(7980, 'en-US', '<h2>1. Introduction to the game Rust</h2><p> Rust, developed by Facepunch Studios, is a popular open-world survival game. In the game, players find themselves on an island where they have to collect resources, build a shelter, and fight other players for survival. One of the important elements of the game is the use of explosives, which are used to hack the bases of other players or protect your base.</p><h2> 2. Types of explosives in Rust</h2><p> Explosives in Rust come in various forms. The main types of explosives available to players are:</p><ul><li> Discharge charges are a basic type of explosive that are used to breach the doors and walls of an enemy base. They are relatively cheap to produce and are available from the very beginning of the game.</li><li> Thermal barrels - this explosive is used to destroy armored doors and walls. It is more expensive and more difficult to produce, but has a greater explosive power than unloading charges.</li><li> Reconnaissance charges - this type of explosive is used to explode drives, boxes and chests. Unlike other types of explosives, the resources obtained by hacking drives are usually insignificant.</li><li> C4 is the most powerful type of explosive in Rust. Its use is only justified for blowing up key objects, such as the main entrances to the base or the base itself as a whole.</li></ul><h2> 3. Use of explosive beds</h2><p> The use of explosive beds is an integral part of the hacking and base defense techniques in the game Rust. Beds consisting of an explosive and a moderator allow players to precisely control the location of the explosion and reduce the risk of accidental detonation due to possible interaction with the game\'s dynamics.</p><p> Proper use of explosive beds can significantly increase the effectiveness of hacking or defending a base. Exploding beds can destroy high-level walls and doors, as well as kill enemy players near the explosion.</p><h2> 4. Efficiency of using beds</h2><p> Using explosive patches can significantly speed up hacking or defending a base in Rust. Beds allow players to choose the optimal location for the explosion and precisely focus damage on important base objects. In addition, the use of beds can provoke panic among opponents and make them less careful.</p><h2> 5. Risks when working with explosives in the game Rust</h2><p> Working with explosives poses certain risks in Rust. Improper use of explosive beds can lead to unwanted consequences, such as accidentally exploding and causing damage to your base or team members. Additionally, using explosives in inappropriate situations can attract the attention of other players and increase the likelihood of an attack.</p><h2> 6. Tips for safe use</h2><p> To safely use explosives in Rust, it is recommended to follow these tips:</p><ul><li> Plan and prepare carefully to hack or defend the base. Assess all risks and possible consequences.</li><li> Use explosive beds to precisely control the location of the explosion and reduce the likelihood of accidental damage.</li><li> Collaborate and communicate with team members while working with explosives.</li><li> Be careful when storing explosives and do not allow unauthorized players to access them.</li><li> Follow the rules and restrictions on the server to avoid being banned or punished for illegal use of explosives.</li></ul><h2> 7. Conclusion</h2><p> Using explosive patches in Rust is essential to successfully hacking or defending a base. Proper use of beds can improve efficiency and reduce the risks of working with explosives. However, you must be careful and follow safety rules to avoid unwanted consequences.</p>'),
