(7984, 'en-US', '<h2>1. Stone thrower</h2><p> Characteristics and features:</p><ul><li> Damage: low</li><li> Attack Speed: High</li><li> Throw range: medium</li></ul><p> Benefits of use:</p><ul><li> Availability: Rocks can be found everywhere, making the rock thrower one of the most accessible weapons.</li><li> Attack Speed: Due to its high attack speed, the Rock Thrower can cause significant damage to the enemy in a short time.</li></ul><p> Flaws:</p><ul><li> Low Damage: The Rock Thrower is a relatively weak weapon and requires several hits to neutralize the enemy.</li><li> Throw Range: Rocks have a limited throw range, which can make it difficult to hit and deal damage.</li></ul><p> Tips for use:</p><ul><li> Use the Rock Thrower to deal damage at close range, especially if you don\'t have access to other melee weapons.</li><li> Aim to hit the enemy\'s head to inflict maximum damage.</li></ul><h2> 2. Machete</h2><p> Characteristics and features:</p><ul><li> Damage: high</li><li> Attack Speed: Medium</li><li> Range: short</li></ul><p> Benefits of use:</p><ul><li> High Damage: The machete is capable of dealing significant damage in a single blow, making it an effective weapon in close combat.</li><li> Versatility: The machete can be used for a variety of tasks, including cutting down trees and chopping rocks.</li></ul><p> Flaws:</p><ul><li> Relative Slowness: The machete\'s attack speed is slower than some other melee weapons, requiring more careful planning and timing to strike.</li></ul><p> Tips for use:</p><ul><li> Try to flank and hit your opponent from behind to maximize damage.</li><li> Remember to adjust the machete accurately after blows so that its durability is not depleted.</li></ul><h2> 3. Pickaxe</h2><p> Characteristics and features:</p><ul><li> Damage: high</li><li> Attack Speed: Low</li><li> Range: short</li></ul><p> Benefits of use:</p><ul><li> Ability to Gather Resources: The pickaxe can be used to collect stones, wood, and metal, making it a useful survival tool in the game.</li><li> High Damage: The pickaxe can deal significant damage to an enemy in one hit.</li></ul><p> Flaws:</p><ul><li> Low Attack Speed: The pickaxe is relatively slow and can be a counter to fast opponents.</li></ul><p> Tips for use:</p><ul><li> Use the pickaxe as a weapon when necessary, but don\'t forget its fundamental role in resource gathering.</li><li> Build shelters and survival tools with a pickaxe.</li></ul><h2> 4. Tailed Dagger</h2><p> Characteristics and features:</p><ul><li> Damage: medium</li><li> Attack Speed: High</li><li> Range: short</li></ul><p> Benefits of use:</p><ul><li> High Attack Speed: The tailed dagger has one of the highest attack speeds among melee weapons, allowing it to deliver multiple hits in a short time.</li><li> Low Noise: Using the tailed dagger makes no noise, allowing you to strike stealthily and avoid attracting attention.</li></ul><p> Flaws:</p><ul><li> Average Damage: The tailed dagger cannot deal as much damage as some other melee weapons.</li></ul><p> Tips for use:</p><ul><li> Use the tailed dagger to sneak attacks and deal quick damage, especially when the enemy is paying attention to you.</li><li> Remember that the tailed dagger is not the best choice for long fights, and it is better to use it in combination with stronger weapons.</li></ul><h2> 5. Shotgun</h2><p> Characteristics and features:</p><ul><li> Damage: high</li><li> Attack Speed: Low</li><li> Range: short</li></ul><p> Benefits of use:</p><ul><li> Very high damage: the shotgun is capable of dealing powerful damage to the nearest enemy and causing serious damage to them.</li><li> Shooting efficiency: the shotgun is widely used for hunting animals and fighting with other players.</li></ul><p> Flaws:</p><ul><li> Long Reload Time: Once fired, the shotgun takes time to reload, leaving you vulnerable if the shot goes wrong.</li><li> Limited Range: Shotguns are only effective at close range and do not have good accuracy at long range.</li></ul><p> Tips for use:</p><ul><li> Aim to shoot at the enemy\'s body to maximize damage.</li><li> Don\'t forget to reload and plan your shotgun use depending on the situation.</li></ul><h2> 6. Rake</h2><p> Characteristics and features:</p><ul><li> Damage: low</li><li> Attack Speed: High</li><li> Range: short</li></ul><p> Benefits of use:</p><ul><li> High Attack Speed: The rake has one of the highest attack speeds among melee weapons, allowing you to land multiple hits in a short time.</li><li> Cheap: The rake is one of the cheapest weapons in Rust.</li></ul><p> Flaws:</p><ul><li> Low Damage: The rake deals limited damage and often requires multiple hits to neutralize the enemy.</li></ul><p> Tips for use:</p><ul><li> Use the rake to deal quick melee damage and even stun your opponent so they can use another weapon or escape.</li><li> Aim to hit the enemy\'s head to increase damage.</li></ul><h2> 7. Spear</h2><p> Characteristics and features:</p><ul><li> Damage: medium</li><li> Attack Speed: Medium</li><li> Range: medium</li></ul><p> Benefits of use:</p><ul><li> Attack Range: Due to its length, the spear can attack opponents at medium range.</li><li> Throwing ability: The spear can be thrown over a distance, causing damage to the enemy.</li></ul><p> Flaws:</p><ul><li> Average Damage: The spear does not have the highest damage, so it may take several hits to neutralize the enemy.</li><li> Limited Effectiveness at Close Range: The spear may be less effective in close combat due to its length and limited striking capabilities.</li></ul><p> Tips for use:</p><ul><li> Use the spear to attack opponents at mid-range and to throw when necessary.</li><li> Aim to hit your opponent\'s head to increase damage.</li></ul><h2> 8. Bow and arrows</h2><p> Characteristics and features:</p><ul><li> Damage: medium</li><li> Attack Speed: Low</li><li> Range: high</li></ul><p> Benefits of use:</p><ul><li> Long Range: The bow and arrows have a long range, allowing them to deal damage to enemies at great distances.</li><li> Quiet Shooting: Using a bow does not cut through noise, making it ideal for sneak attacks.</li></ul><p> Flaws:</p><ul><li> Slow Attack Speed: The bow takes time to draw, making it less effective during emergency situations.</li><li> Requires a Hit: Dealing damage to an enemy requires precision and hitting the target.</li></ul><p> Tips for use:</p><ul><li> Use the bow for long-range sneak attacks or to hunt animals.</li><li> Practice precision and aim to shoot your opponent\'s head.</li></ul><h2> 9. Spiral steel</h2><p> Characteristics and features:</p><ul><li> Damage: high</li><li> Attack Speed: Medium</li><li> Range: short</li></ul><p> Benefits of use:</p><ul><li> Power Strike: Spiral Steel is capable of causing significant damage to an opponent with a single powerful strike.</li><li> Stability: Spiral steel is highly durable, making it a durable weapon.</li></ul><p> Flaws:</p><ul><li> Limited Range: Spiral Steel is only effective at close range and can be difficult to counter against opponents at a greater distance.</li></ul><p> Tips for use:</p><ul><li> Use Spiral Steel to deliver powerful melee attacks and harden heavily armored opponents.</li><li> Try to deliver a fatal blow to the enemy\'s head.</li></ul><h2> 10. Hammer</h2><p> Characteristics and features:</p><ul><li> Damage: high</li><li> Attack Speed: Low</li><li> Range: short</li></ul><p> Benefits of use:</p><ul><li> Powerful Damage: The hammer is capable of inflicting very high damage on an opponent with one powerful blow.</li><li> Good breaking ability: the hammer can break parts of the enemy\'s armor and make him more vulnerable.</li></ul><p> Flaws:</p><ul><li> Slow Attack Speed: Using the hammer takes time to draw, making it less effective during fast fights.</li></ul><p> Tips for use:</p><ul><li> Use the hammer to deliver powerful blows and break enemy armor.</li><li> Aim to hit the enemy\'s head to increase damage.</li></ul><h2> How to choose the right bladed weapon</h2><p> Choosing the right melee weapon in Rust depends on several factors:</p><ul><li> Playstyle: If you prefer active and fast combat, then melee weapons such as the Rock Thrower or Tailed Dagger may be a better choice. If you are prone to sneak attacks and ranged combat, then a bow and arrow or spear may be more suitable.</li><li> Available Resources: Some melee weapons require more materials and time to craft than others. Consider your resources and capabilities before making a decision.</li><li> Weapon Stats: Study the stats of each weapon and determine which aspects are important to you. For example, if you need a weapon with high damage, then a machete or hammer may be a better choice.</li><li> Situation and Environment: Consider the situation in which you are using the weapon, as well as the environment in which you are located. Some weapons are more effective in close combat, while others work well at long ranges.</li></ul><h2> Conclusion</h2><p> The game Rust offers many options for melee weapons, each of which has its own characteristics and purpose. Choosing the right melee weapon can have a significant impact on your effectiveness in combat and your playstyle. Familiarize yourself with the characteristics of each weapon, study their advantages and disadvantages, and choose the weapon that suits your needs and preferences. Good luck in your battles in the world of Rust!</p>'),
