(17877, 'en-US', 'Play on the best Rust servers with unique settings and a friendly community. Join Prostoj today!'),
(17878, 'en-US', 'Rust servers, Rust game servers, Rust multiplayer, Rust play online, Rust servers with mods, Rust servers with low ping, Rust servers with a friendly community, Rust servers with wipe, Rust servers with unique settings, Rust servers for beginners'),
(17879, 'en-US', 'This user agreement (hereinafter referred to as the \"User Agreement\") governs the relationship regarding the use of the Prostoj service via a website on the Internet (hereinafter referred to as the \"Network\") with the address https://'),
(17880, 'en-US', ' between (hereinafter referred to as the “System” - “Contractor”) and an adult individual (hereinafter referred to as the “User”).'),
(17881, 'en-US', '1. Subject of the User Agreement'),
(17882, 'en-US', 'The Contractor offers the User the Prostoj service on the terms and conditions that are the subject of this User Agreement (hereinafter referred to as the UA). The User Agreement may be amended without any special notice.'),
(17883, 'en-US', '2. Description of the service'),
(17884, 'en-US', 'Prostoj is an automated interface for accepting voluntary donations using a web interface located only at https://'),
(17885, 'en-US', ' and on the accompanying pages.'),
(17886, 'en-US', 'The Prostoj service is provided to Users who have access to the Internet.'),
(17887, 'en-US', '3. Entry into force of the User Agreement'),
(17888, 'en-US', 'The User Agreement comes into force upon the User expressing consent to its terms in the form of the User clicking the “I accept the terms” button.'),
(17889, 'en-US', '4. User Conduct'),
(17890, 'en-US', 'The User understands and accepts that the Contractor bears no responsibility for actions related to the use of the Prostoj service. The Contractor does not control the volumes of transfers of electronic units made using the Prostoj service and does not guarantee their accuracy and completeness. The User understands that by using the Prostoj service, the User acts at his own risk. Under no circumstances will the Contractor be liable for the User\'s actions within the Prostoj service.'),
(17891, 'en-US', 'The User understands that access to the service, as well as the provision of any information, depends on a number of technical prerequisites that are partially outside the scope of activity and influence of the Contractor. If the service is unavailable, the Contractor bears no liability if this violation is caused by a reason that is outside the Contractor\'s area of responsibility. The behavior of the Contractor\'s partners in providing the Prostoj service provided for by this UA cannot be attributed to the Contractor in any way.'),
(17892, 'en-US', 'The User undertakes not to place any advertisements of the Contractor without the consent of the Contractor.'),
(17893, 'en-US', '5. General provisions on use'),
(17894, 'en-US', 'The User acknowledges that the Contractor may set restrictions on the use of the Prostoj service. The Contractor shall not be liable for any delays, failures, incorrect or untimely processing of the User\'s transactions.'),
(17895, 'en-US', 'The User acknowledges that the Contractor may change the rules and restrictions at any time, with or without prior notice.'),
(17896, 'en-US', 'The User transfers to the Contractor, free of charge, monetary funds in the amount proposed by the Contractor.'),
(17897, 'en-US', 'The Contractor does not take part in possible disagreements and disputes (including legal ones) between Users and Customers.'),
(17898, 'en-US', 'The Contractor does not guarantee permanent or unconditional access to the Prostoj service. The functioning of the Prostoj service may be disrupted by force majeure and other factors, the prevention or overcoming of which is beyond the Contractor\'s capabilities.'),
(17899, 'en-US', 'No information or advice given by the Contractor can be considered as a guarantee, since they are consultations, but not a technical way to ensure the provision of the Prostoj service.'),
(17900, 'en-US', 'The Contractor shall not be liable for the compatibility of the Prostoj service with the User\'s data, programs, configurations and other hardware and software resources. In particular, the Contractor shall not bear any costs, payments, expenses incurred by the User for integration or failed integration of the Prostoj service. Any liability for damages arising from the fact that a third party has illegally used the User\'s access is also excluded.'),
(17901, 'en-US', 'The Contractor does not guarantee that the Prostoj service will be provided without interruption or without errors. Under no circumstances will the Contractor be liable for direct or indirect damage caused to the User as a result of the use or inability to use the Prostoj service; or incurred as a result of errors, omissions, interruptions in work, deletion of files, defects, delays in work or data transmission.'),
(17902, 'en-US', 'The Contractor reserves the right to improve or modify the Prostoj service at any time.'),
(17903, 'en-US', 'A User who is not satisfied with the Prostoj service, its terms, rules, quality, content or practice of providing the service has the exclusive right of the User to stop using the Prostoj service until the User clicks the “I accept the terms” button.'),
(17904, 'en-US', 'If the Contractor has sufficient grounds to believe that the service is being used for illegal purposes, the User\'s access may be blocked.'),
(17905, 'en-US', 'The User undertakes not to use the Prostoj service for purposes that may cause direct or indirect damage to third parties. It is also prohibited to use the service for the purpose of inciting hatred or hostility, as well as to humiliate the dignity of a person or group of persons on the basis of gender, race, nationality, language, origin, attitude to religion, as well as belonging to any social group, calls for extremist activity and for other illegal purposes. In the event that such facts are established, the User\'s access may be blocked.'),
(17906, 'en-US', '6. Termination of the Prostoj service'),
(17907, 'en-US', 'The Contractor, without bearing legal liability and without compensating the User for any losses, has the right to unilaterally, through the website https://'),
(17908, 'en-US', ', terminate the provision of the Prostoj service to the User in the following cases:'),
(17909, 'en-US', 'The Contractor has suspicions that the User is committing or has committed illegal actions using the Prostoj service.'),
(17910, 'en-US', 'The Contractor suspects or has discovered that the User has attempted, is, or has sent a large number of HTTP requests to the Prostoj service.'),
(17911, 'en-US', 'The Contractor has grounds to consider further cooperation with the User undesirable.'),
(17912, 'en-US', 'The Contractor has reason to believe that further cooperation with the User is unworthy, inappropriate, damaging or even detrimental to the name or reputation of the Contractor.'),
(17913, 'en-US', 'The User commits a legally punishable, unfair or unethical action against the Contractor or an action that affects the interests or reputation of the Contractor or third parties.'),
(17914, 'en-US', 'The User in any way compromises the Contractor, or commits a humiliating, offensive or slanderous act towards the Contractor or its employees.'),
(17915, 'en-US', 'The information provided by the User is inaccurate, or the Contractor has suspicions that such information is inaccurate.'),
(17916, 'en-US', 'In case of using the service not for its intended purpose.'),
(17917, 'en-US', 'In other cases provided for by this PS.'),
(17918, 'en-US', '7. Duration and termination of the agreement'),
(17919, 'en-US', 'The term of this PS begins from the moment the User applies to the Prostoj service and ends at the moment of termination of the PS.'),
(17920, 'en-US', 'The Contractor has the right to terminate relations with the User in the event of the latter’s violation of this User Agreement.'),
(17921, 'en-US', 'The Contractor is not obliged to store the User\'s data after the termination of the Agreement with the User and the performance of actions using the Prostoj service.'),
(17922, 'en-US', '8. General information'),
(17923, 'en-US', 'Unless otherwise provided by an additional agreement between the User and the Contractor, all claims, requests, questions, and any other correspondence must be sent to the Contractor by email at help@Prostoj.ru.'),
(17924, 'en-US', 'The PS is a legally binding agreement between the User and the Contractor and regulates the User\'s use of the Prostoj service.'),
(17925, 'en-US', 'The recognition by a court of any provision of the Agreement as invalid or unenforceable shall not entail the invalidity or unenforceability of other provisions of the Agreement.'),
(17926, 'en-US', 'Inaction on the part of the Contractor in the event of a violation by the User or other users of the provisions of the User Agreement does not deprive the Contractor of the right to take appropriate actions to protect its interests later.'),
(17927, 'en-US', '9. Return of digital goods'),
(17928, 'en-US', 'The goods purchased on this site are intangible and therefore cannot be physically returned, therefore the digital goods purchased are non-returnable.'),
(17929, 'en-US', 'The reason for the return of funds spent on the purchase of a product may be an irreparable problem in the operation of this product.'),
(17930, 'en-US', 'If a purchaser of a digital product claims that it is not working, the support service may require verification of this by requesting remote access to the computer on which the purchased digital product was installed.'),
(17931, 'en-US', 'Editorial from 24.12.2020'),
(17932, 'en-US', 'This user agreement (hereinafter referred to as the \"User Agreement\") governs the relationship regarding the use of the service through a website on the Internet (hereinafter referred to as the \"Network\") with the address https://'),
(17933, 'en-US', 'The Contractor offers the User the service on the terms and conditions that are the subject of this User Agreement (hereinafter referred to as the UA). The User Agreement may be amended without any special notice.'),
(17934, 'en-US', 'is an automated interface for accepting voluntary donations using a web interface located only at https://'),
(17935, 'en-US', 'The service is provided to Users who have access to the Internet.'),
(17936, 'en-US', 'The User understands and accepts that the Contractor bears no responsibility for actions related to the use of the service. The Contractor does not control the volumes of transfers of electronic units that occur using the service and does not guarantee their accuracy and completeness. The User understands that by using the service, the User acts at his own risk. Under no circumstances will the Contractor be liable for the actions of the User within the service.'),
(17937, 'en-US', 'The User understands that access to the service, as well as the provision of any information, depends on a number of technical prerequisites that are partially outside the scope of activity and influence of the Contractor. If the service is unavailable, the Contractor bears no liability if this violation is caused by a reason that is outside the Contractor\'s area of responsibility. The behavior of the Contractor\'s partners in providing the service provided for by this User Agreement cannot be attributed to the Contractor in any way.'),
(17938, 'en-US', 'The User acknowledges that the Contractor may impose restrictions on the use of the service. The Contractor shall not be liable for any delays, failures, incorrect or untimely processing of the User\'s transactions.'),
(17939, 'en-US', 'The Contractor does not guarantee permanent or unconditional access to the service. The functioning of the service may be disrupted by force majeure and other factors, the prevention or overcoming of which is beyond the capabilities of the Contractor.'),
(17940, 'en-US', 'No information or advice given by the Contractor can be considered as a guarantee, since they are consultations, but not a technical way of ensuring the provision of the service.'),
(17941, 'en-US', 'The Contractor shall not be liable for the compatibility of the service with the User\'s data, programs, configurations and other hardware and software resources. In particular, the Contractor shall not bear any costs, payments, expenses incurred by the User for integration or failed integration of the service. Any liability for damages arising from the fact that a third party has illegally used the User\'s access is also excluded.'),
(17942, 'en-US', 'The Contractor does not guarantee that the service will be provided without interruption or without errors. Under no circumstances will the Contractor be liable for direct or indirect damage caused to the User as a result of the use or inability to use the service; or incurred as a result of errors, omissions, interruptions in work, deletion of files, defects, delays in work or data transmission.'),
(17943, 'en-US', 'The Contractor reserves the right to improve or modify the service at any time.'),
(17944, 'en-US', 'A User who is not satisfied with the service, terms, rules, quality, its content or the practice of providing the service has the exclusive right of the User to stop using the service before the User clicks the “I accept the terms” button.'),
(17945, 'en-US', 'The User undertakes not to use the service for purposes that may cause direct or indirect damage to third parties. It is also prohibited to use the service for the purpose of inciting hatred or hostility, as well as to humiliate the dignity of a person or group of persons on the basis of gender, race, nationality, language, origin, attitude to religion, as well as belonging to any social group, calls for extremist activity and for other illegal purposes. In the event that such facts are established, the User\'s access may be blocked.'),
(17946, 'en-US', '6. Termination of service'),
(17947, 'en-US', ', terminate the provision of the service to the User in the following cases:'),
(17948, 'en-US', 'The Contractor has suspicions that the User is committing or has committed illegal actions using the service.'),
(17949, 'en-US', 'The Contractor suspects or has discovered that the User has attempted, is, or has sent a large number of HTTP requests to the service.'),
(17950, 'en-US', 'The term of this PS begins from the moment the User applies to the service and ends at the moment of termination of the PS.'),
(17951, 'en-US', 'The Contractor is not obliged to store the User\'s data after the termination of the Agreement with the User and the performance of actions using the service.'),
(17952, 'en-US', 'Unless otherwise provided by an additional agreement between the User and the Contractor, all claims, requests, questions, and any other correspondence must be sent to the Contractor by e-mail'),
(17953, 'en-US', 'The PS is a legally binding agreement between the User and the Contractor and regulates the User’s use of the service.'),
(17954, 'en-US', 'Personal data protection policy'),
(17955, 'en-US', 'This Regulation is governed by the Constitution of the Russian Federation, the Federal Law \"On Information, Information Technologies and the Protection of Information\" No. 149-FZ of July 27, 2006, the Federal Law \"On Personal Data\" No. 152-FZ of July 27, 2006 and other regulatory legal acts.'),
(17956, 'en-US', '1. General Provisions'),
(17957, 'en-US', 'The main concepts used in the Regulation:'),
(17958, 'en-US', 'An online store is a website that sells goods via the Internet. It allows users to place an order for purchase online, in their browser, select a method of payment and delivery of the order, and pay for the order.'),
(17959, 'en-US', 'Client – an individual, a consumer of the online store’s services, and a subject of personal data.'),
(17960, 'en-US', 'Personal data – information stored in any format, related to a specific or determinable on the basis of such information natural person (subject of personal data), which by itself or in combination with other information available to the online store allows to identify the identity of the Client.'),
(17961, 'en-US', 'Processing of personal data – actions (operations) with personal data, including collection, systematization, accumulation, storage, clarification (updating, modification), use, distribution (including transfer), depersonalization, blocking, destruction of personal data.'),
(17962, 'en-US', 'Dissemination of personal data – actions aimed at transferring personal data to a certain circle of persons (transfer of personal data) or familiarizing an unlimited circle of persons with personal data, including disclosure of personal data in the media, posting in information and telecommunications networks or providing access to personal data in any other way.'),
(17963, 'en-US', 'Use of personal data – actions (operations) with personal data performed by the operator for the purpose of making decisions or performing other actions that generate legal consequences in relation to the subject of personal data or other persons or otherwise affect the rights and freedoms of the subject of personal data or other persons.'),
(17964, 'en-US', 'Confidentiality of personal data is a mandatory requirement for the operator or other person who has access to personal data to prevent their dissemination without the consent of the subject of the personal data or the presence of another legal basis.'),
(17965, 'en-US', 'This Regulation establishes the procedure for processing the personal data of Clients, users of the Seller’s online store, presented on the website “https://prostoj.store/”, including subdomains.'),
(17966, 'en-US', 'The purpose of the Regulation is to ensure the protection of the rights and freedoms of a person and citizen when processing his personal data.'),
(17967, 'en-US', 'Personal data is processed for the purpose of fulfilling the contract of sale of goods of the online store, one of the parties to which is the Client. The online store collects data only to the extent necessary to achieve the said purpose.'),
(17968, 'en-US', 'Personal data may not be used for the purpose of causing property or moral harm to citizens or hindering the exercise of the rights and freedoms of citizens of the Russian Federation.'),
(17969, 'en-US', 'This Regulation is approved by the General Director M.V. Kobilyansky and is mandatory for all employees who have access to the Client’s personal data.'),
(17970, 'en-US', '2. Composition and receipt of personal data of Clients'),
(17971, 'en-US', 'Personal data collected and processed by the online store includes:'),
(17972, 'en-US', 'other data specified by the Client when placing an order.'),
(17973, 'en-US', 'All personal data is received by online store employees directly from the subject of personal data – Clients.'),
(17974, 'en-US', '3. Processing and storage of personal data of Clients'),
(17975, 'en-US', 'The processing of personal data by the online store in the interests of Clients consists of receiving, systematizing, accumulating, storing, clarifying (updating, changing), using, distributing, depersonalizing, blocking, destroying and protecting from unauthorized access.'),
(17976, 'en-US', 'The consent of Clients to the processing of personal data is not required, since the processing of personal data is carried out for the purpose of fulfilling the purchase and sale agreement, one of the parties to which is the subject of personal data - the Client.'),
(17977, 'en-US', 'The processing of personal data of Clients is carried out using the mixed processing method.'),
(17978, 'en-US', 'Only employees of the online store who are authorized to work with the Client\'s personal data and who have signed the Agreement on Non-Disclosure of the Client\'s Personal Data may have access to the processing of the Client\'s personal data.'),
(17979, 'en-US', 'The list of employees of the online store who have access to the personal data of Clients is determined by the order of the General Director Kobilyansky M.V.'),
(17980, 'en-US', 'The storage period of personal data of the Clients of the online store is determined by Article 196 of the Civil Code of the Russian Federation \"General limitation period\" and is three years after the termination of the purchase and sale agreement.'),
(17981, 'en-US', 'Personal data of Clients is stored in electronic form in the local computer network of the online store.'),
(17982, 'en-US', '4. Use and transfer of personal data of Clients'),
(17983, 'en-US', 'The use of personal data of Clients is carried out by the online store solely for the achievement of the goals defined in the purchase and sale agreement between the Client and the online store, in particular, for the sale and delivery of goods, as well as additional services.'),
(17984, 'en-US', 'When transferring personal data of Clients, the online store must comply with the following requirements:'),
(17985, 'en-US', 'Warn persons receiving personal data of Clients that this data may be used only for the purposes for which it was communicated, and require these persons to confirm that this rule has been observed. Persons receiving personal data of Clients are obliged to observe the confidentiality regime. This provision does not apply in the case of anonymization of personal data and in relation to publicly available data.'),
(17986, 'en-US', 'Allow access to personal data of Clients only to specially authorized persons, and such persons must have the right to receive only those personal data that are necessary to perform specific functions.'),
(17987, 'en-US', 'It is not permitted to answer questions related to the transfer of information containing personal data by telephone or fax.'),
(17988, 'en-US', 'The online store has the right to provide or transfer personal data of Clients to third parties in the following cases:'),
(17989, 'en-US', 'If disclosure of this information is required to comply with the law, or to execute a judicial act;'),
(17990, 'en-US', 'To assist in investigations carried out by law enforcement or other government agencies;'),
(17991, 'en-US', 'To protect the legal rights of the Client and the online store;'),
(17992, 'en-US', 'To fulfill the requirements of the sales contract concluded with the Client, including the delivery of goods using the services of contractors (including the transfer of information to courier or postal delivery services).'),
(17993, 'en-US', '5. Protection of personal data of Clients from unauthorized access'),
(17994, 'en-US', 'When processing personal data of Clients, the online store is obliged to take the necessary organizational and technical measures to protect personal data from unauthorized or accidental access, destruction, modification, blocking, copying, distribution of personal data, as well as from other illegal actions.'),
(17995, 'en-US', 'To effectively protect the personal data of Clients, it is necessary:'),
(17996, 'en-US', 'Comply with the procedure for receiving, recording and storing personal data of Clients;'),
(17997, 'en-US', 'Use technical means of security and signaling;'),
(17998, 'en-US', 'Conclude a Non-Disclosure Agreement with all employees involved in the receipt, processing and protection of the Client’s personal data;'),
(17999, 'en-US', 'Bring to disciplinary responsibility employees guilty of violating the rules governing the receipt, processing and protection of the Client\'s personal data.'),
(18000, 'en-US', 'Access to personal data of Clients by employees of the online store who do not have properly executed access is prohibited.'),
(18001, 'en-US', 'Protection of access to electronic databases containing personal data of Clients is ensured by:'),
(18002, 'en-US', 'Using licensed software products that prevent unauthorized access by third parties to the personal data of Clients;'),
(18003, 'en-US', 'Password system. Passwords are set by the system administrator and communicated individually to employees who have access to the personal data of Clients.'),
(18004, 'en-US', 'Copying and making extracts of the Client\'s personal data is permitted exclusively for official purposes with the written permission of the General Director M.V. Kobilyansky.'),
(18005, 'en-US', '6. Responsibilities of the online store'),
(18006, 'en-US', 'Process personal data of Clients solely for the purpose of providing legitimate services to Clients.'),
(18007, 'en-US', 'Obtain personal data of the Client directly from him or her or via the website. If the Client\'s personal data can only be obtained from a third party, the Client must be notified of this in advance and written consent must be obtained from him. Employees of the online store must inform Clients of the purposes, intended sources and methods of obtaining personal data, as well as the nature of the personal data to be obtained and the consequences of the client\'s refusal to give written consent to receive it.'),
(18008, 'en-US', 'Not to receive or process the Client’s personal data about his/her race, nationality, political views, religious or philosophical beliefs, health status, intimate life, except in cases provided by law.'),
(18009, 'en-US', 'Provide access to their personal data to the Client or their legal representative upon request or upon receipt of a request containing the number of the main identity document of the Client or their legal representative, information on the date of issue of the said document and the issuing authority, and the personal signature of the Client or their legal representative. The request may be sent electronically and signed with an electronic digital signature in accordance with the legislation of the Russian Federation. Information on the availability of personal data must be provided to the Client in an accessible form and must not contain personal data related to other subjects of personal data.'),
(18010, 'en-US', 'Limit the Client’s right to access his/her personal data if:'),
(18011, 'en-US', 'The processing of personal data, including personal data obtained as a result of operational-search, counterintelligence and intelligence activities, is carried out for the purposes of national defense, state security and the protection of law and order;'),
(18012, 'en-US', 'The processing of personal data is carried out by the bodies that have detained the subject of personal data on suspicion of committing a crime or brought charges against the subject of personal data in a criminal case, or applied a preventive measure to the subject of personal data prior to the presentation of charges, with the exception of cases provided for by the criminal procedure legislation of the Russian Federation, if the suspect or accused is allowed to become familiar with such personal data;'),
(18013, 'en-US', 'Providing personal data violates the constitutional rights and freedoms of others.'),
(18014, 'en-US', 'Ensure the storage and protection of the Client’s personal data from unauthorized use or loss.'),
(18015, 'en-US', 'In the event of detection of inaccurate personal data or illegal actions with them by the operator upon request or at the request of the subject of personal data or his legal representative or the authorized body for the protection of the rights of subjects of personal data, the operator is obliged to block the personal data related to the relevant subject of personal data, from the moment of such request or receipt of such request for the verification period.'),
(18016, 'en-US', 'In the event of confirmation of the fact that personal data is inaccurate, the operator, on the basis of documents submitted by the subject of personal data or his legal representative or the authorized body for the protection of the rights of subjects of personal data, or other necessary documents, is obliged to clarify the personal data and remove their blocking.'),
(18017, 'en-US', 'In the event of detection of illegal actions with personal data, the operator is obliged to eliminate the violations committed within a period not exceeding three working days from the date of such detection. In the event that it is impossible to eliminate the violations committed, the operator is obliged to destroy the personal data within a period not exceeding three working days from the date of detection of illegal actions with personal data. The operator is obliged to notify the subject of personal data or his legal representative of the elimination of the violations committed or the destruction of personal data, and in the event that the appeal or request was sent by the authorized body for the protection of the rights of subjects of personal data, also the said body.'),
(18018, 'en-US', 'In the event that the purpose of processing personal data is achieved, the operator is obliged to immediately stop processing personal data and destroy the relevant personal data within a period not exceeding three working days from the date of achieving the purpose of processing personal data, unless otherwise provided by federal laws, and notify the subject of personal data or his legal representative of this, and in the event that the appeal or request was sent by the authorized body for the protection of the rights of subjects of personal data, also the said body.'),
(18019, 'en-US', '7. Client Rights'),
(18020, 'en-US', 'Access to information about oneself, including information confirming the fact of personal data processing, as well as the purpose of such processing; methods of personal data processing used by the online store; information about persons who have access to personal data or who may be granted such access; a list of personal data processed and the source of their receipt, the terms of processing personal data, including the terms of their storage; information about what legal consequences for the Client may result from the processing of his personal data.'),
(18021, 'en-US', 'Determination of the forms and methods of processing his personal data.'),
(18022, 'en-US', 'Restriction of methods and forms of personal data processing.'),
(18023, 'en-US', 'Prohibition of distribution of personal data without his consent.'),
(18024, 'en-US', 'Changing, clarifying, destroying information about oneself.'),
(18025, 'en-US', '8. Confidentiality of personal data of Clients'),
(18026, 'en-US', 'Information about the personal data of Clients is confidential.'),
(18027, 'en-US', 'The online store ensures the confidentiality of personal data and is obliged to prevent its distribution to third parties without the consent of the Clients or the presence of other legal grounds.'),
(18028, 'en-US', 'Persons who have access to personal data of Clients are obliged to observe the confidentiality regime, they must be warned about the need to observe the secrecy regime. In connection with the confidentiality regime of personal information, appropriate security measures must be provided to protect data from accidental or unauthorized destruction, accidental loss, unauthorized access to them, modification or distribution.'),
(18029, 'en-US', 'All confidentiality measures during the collection, processing and storage of personal data of Clients apply to all information carriers, both paper and automated.'),
(18030, 'en-US', 'The confidentiality regime of personal data is lifted in cases of depersonalization or inclusion of personal data in publicly available sources, unless otherwise specified by law.'),
(18031, 'en-US', '9. Responsibility for violation of the rules governing the processing of personal data of Clients'),
(18032, 'en-US', 'The online store is responsible for the personal information that is in its possession and establishes the personal responsibility of employees for compliance with the established confidentiality regime.'),
(18033, 'en-US', 'Each employee who receives a document containing the Client\'s personal data for work is solely responsible for the safety of the medium and the confidentiality of the information.'),
(18034, 'en-US', 'Any person may contact the management of the online store with a complaint about the violation of this Regulation. Complaints and applications regarding compliance with data processing requirements are considered within 5 days from the date of receipt.'),
(18035, 'en-US', 'The employees of the online store are obliged to ensure that requests, applications and complaints from Clients are considered at the proper level, and also to facilitate the implementation of the requirements of the competent authorities.'),
(18036, 'en-US', 'Persons guilty of violating the rules governing the receipt, processing and protection of personal data of Clients shall bear disciplinary, administrative, civil or criminal liability in accordance with federal laws.'),
(18037, 'en-US', 'This Privacy Policy (hereinafter referred to as the Policy) is an appendix to the User Agreement and defines the procedure for processing and protecting personal information about Users that the service (hereinafter referred to as the “Administration”) may receive during their use of the Administration Service (hereinafter referred to as the Services).'),
(18038, 'en-US', 'Before using the Service, users should read the terms of this Privacy Policy.'),
(18039, 'en-US', 'Use of the Service in any form means the User\'s unconditional consent to the terms of this Privacy Policy and the terms of processing of his/her personal information specified therein. In case of disagreement with the terms of the Privacy Policy, the User must refrain from using the Service.'),
(18040, 'en-US', 'The Privacy Policy (including any of its parts) may be changed by the Administration without any special notice and without paying any compensation in connection therewith. The new version of the Privacy Policy comes into force from the moment it is posted on the Administration\'s website.'),
(18041, 'en-US', 'By accepting the terms of this Policy, the User expresses his/her consent to the processing of the User\'s data by the Administration for the purposes provided for in this Policy, as well as to the transfer of the User\'s data to third parties in the cases listed in this Policy.'),
(18042, 'en-US', 'The specified consent may be revoked by the User only if he/she notifies the Administration in writing at least 180 days prior to the expected date of termination of the use of the data by the Administration.'),
(18043, 'en-US', 'Using the Service with a web browser that accepts data from cookies means that the User expresses his/her consent to the Administration collecting and processing data from cookies for the purposes specified in this Policy, as well as to the transfer of data from cookies to third parties in the cases listed in this Policy.'),
(18044, 'en-US', 'Disabling and/or blocking by the User of the web browser option for receiving data from cookies means a ban on the collection and processing of data from cookies by the Administration in accordance with the terms of this Privacy Policy.'),
(18045, 'en-US', '1.4. As a general rule, the Administration does not check the veracity of the personal information provided by Users. However, in cases stipulated by the User Agreement, the User is obliged to provide confirmation of the veracity of the personal information provided by him/her.'),
(18046, 'en-US', '2. Composition of information about Users that is received and processed by the Administration'),
(18047, 'en-US', 'This Policy applies to the following types of personal information:'),
(18048, 'en-US', 'Personal information posted by Users, including about themselves when filling out the form to send a message, other personal information, access to which the User provides to the Administration through websites or services of third parties, or personal information posted by Users in the process of using the Service. Personal information obtained in this way may include, in particular, the User\'s last name, first name, telephone number, email address, address for order delivery. Other information is provided by the User at his/her discretion.'),
(18049, 'en-US', 'The User is prohibited from providing personal data of third parties without permission from third parties for such distribution or if such personal data of third parties was not received by the User from publicly available sources of information.'),
(18050, 'en-US', 'This Policy also applies to candidates for existing vacancies of the Administration, along with other Users. Candidates for vacancies, sending a resume to the Administration using the Service or by e-mail, for the purpose of passing an interview and further employment, thereby express consent to the processing of the following personal data: last name, first name, patronymic, date of birth, citizenship, city of residence, contacts (phone, e-mail address), places of work and dates of work, as well as other data specified by candidates for vacancies in their resumes.'),
(18051, 'en-US', 'The Seller guarantees the Buyer to maintain the confidentiality of the following personal information about the Buyer:'),
(18052, 'en-US', '— information about the user card;'),
(18053, 'en-US', '— information about purchases and orders.'),
(18054, 'en-US', 'The specified information is transferred by the Seller to third parties solely for the purpose of making payment for the order via the payment system or making a payment to the user\'s card; other cases of transferring the specified information to third parties are not permitted.'),
(18055, 'en-US', 'Data automatically transferred to the Service during their use with the help of software installed on the User’s device, including IP address, individual network number of the device (MAC address, device ID), electronic serial number (IMEI, MEID), data from cookies, information about the browser, operating system, access time, and the User’s search queries.'),
(18056, 'en-US', 'Data additionally provided by Users at the request of the Administration for the purpose of fulfilling the obligations of the Administration to Users regarding the use of the Service.'),
(18057, 'en-US', 'Other information about Users, the collection and/or processing of which is established by the Administration\'s user agreement.'),
(18058, 'en-US', '3. Purposes of collecting and processing information about Users'),
(18059, 'en-US', 'The Administration may use Users\' personal information for the following purposes:'),
(18060, 'en-US', 'Identification of the party within the framework of agreements between the User and the Administration.'),
(18061, 'en-US', 'Providing Users with services using the Service and to fulfill its obligations to them, including clarifying payment details, processing orders and requests, and further improving the Service, developing new services and features.'),
(18062, 'en-US', 'Informing Users about the appearance of new materials on the Site, sending requests regarding the use of the Service, and feedback with the User.'),
(18063, 'en-US', 'Carrying out marketing tasks, conducting statistical and other research based on anonymized data.'),
(18064, 'en-US', 'Informing the User via electronic mailings. By providing their data, the User agrees to receive advertising and informational messages and service messages (mailing).'),
(18065, 'en-US', 'Mobile applications may collect anonymous data about the user\'s location in order to provide more correct work with the choice of payment method. Mobile applications may collect anonymous usage statistics.'),
(18066, 'en-US', 'The User hereby expresses his/her consent to the transfer of personal information about him/her to the Administration’s partners and third parties for the purposes specified in paragraph 3.1 of this Privacy Policy.'),
(18067, 'en-US', 'If it is necessary to use personal information about the User for purposes not provided for in this Policy, the Administration requests the User’s consent to such actions.'),
(18068, 'en-US', '4. Processing of information about Users'),
(18069, 'en-US', 'Personal information about Users is stored in accordance with applicable law.'),
(18070, 'en-US', 'Personal information about Users is not transferred to third parties, except in the following cases:'),
(18071, 'en-US', 'The user has consented to such actions.'),
(18072, 'en-US', 'The transfer is necessary to ensure the functioning of the Service and/or its individual functionalities.'),
(18073, 'en-US', 'The transfer is provided for by applicable law.');
INSERT INTO `language_translate` (`id`, `language`, `translation`) VALUES
(18074, 'en-US', 'In order to ensure the possibility of protecting the rights and legitimate interests of the Administration and/or third parties in cases where the User violates the terms of the user agreement.'),
(18075, 'en-US', 'If the Administration participates in a merger, acquisition or any other form of sale of part or all of its assets. In this case, all obligations to comply with the terms of this Policy shall be transferred to the acquirer of the Administration\'s assets.'),
(18076, 'en-US', 'The User is hereby notified and agrees that the Administration may receive personal data of third parties, which are provided by the User when using the Service and use them to implement individual functions of the Service, provided that the User guarantees the consent of third parties, the data about which is provided by the User when using the Service, to be processed by the Administration for the purposes provided for in this Policy, as well as to transfer such data in the cases listed in this Policy.'),
(18077, 'en-US', 'In addition, the User is hereby notified and agrees that the Administration may receive statistical anonymized (without reference to the User) data on the User’s actions when using the Service.'),
(18078, 'en-US', 'Users have the right, upon request, to receive from the Administration information concerning the processing of their personal data.'),
(18079, 'en-US', '5. Measures to protect information about Users'),
(18080, 'en-US', 'The Administration takes all necessary and sufficient organizational and technical measures to protect personal information about Users from unauthorized or accidental access to them, destruction, modification, blocking, distribution of personal information, as well as from other illegal actions with it. These measures include, in particular, internal verification of the processes of collection, storage and processing of data and security measures, including measures to ensure physical security of data to prevent unauthorized access to personal information.'),
(18081, 'en-US', 'This Regulation establishes the procedure for processing personal data of Clients, users of the Seller\'s online store, presented on the website'),
(18082, 'en-US', 'including subdomains.'),
(18083, 'en-US', 'Top players on the server {PARAM_SERVER_NAME_SHORT} Rust! Find out who became the Best Raider, Best Killer, Best Peaceful Player, Top Online, Best Farmer, Best Fisherman, Best Hunter and Best Farmer. See the ratings, follow the leaders and get inspired by their achievements on the server {PARAM_SERVER_NAME} Rust!'),
(18084, 'en-US', 'Player {PARAM_USERNAME}\'s statistics on the server {PARAM_SERVER_NAME_SHORT} Rust. Find out everything about his successes: the number of kills, deaths, collected resources (farm), participation in the team and other key indicators. Follow the player\'s progress and achievements on the server {PARAM_SERVER_NAME} Rust!'),
(18085, 'en-US', 'A list of all our Rust servers with detailed descriptions, wipe dates, and IP addresses. Find out when the next wipe is, connect to your favorite server, and start playing today!'),
(18086, 'en-US', 'Check out the best player-made Rust builds! On this page, you can post your creations, rate other players\' work, and find inspiration for new projects. Show off your building skills, get community recognition, and learn how unique bases, forts, and structures are created in Rust!'),
(18087, 'en-US', 'Earn money by playing on our Rust servers! Learn all about the referral system: attract new players, get bonuses and unique rewards. Streamers and bloggers - get special conditions for monetizing your content. Start earning today by playing Rust on our servers!'),
