(18126, 'en-US', 'Solution for the error \"Infinite Downloading World 0.0%\" or crash with \"Couldn\'t level rust\"'),
(18127, 'en-US', '<p>If Rust freezes on loading the world (Downloading World 0.0%) or crashes with the error \"Couldn\'t level rust\", the problem may be related to the blocking of Cloudflare servers in Russia. In this article, we discuss the causes and solutions, including the use of a VPN, as well as alternative methods for entering our servers.</p>'),
(18128, 'en-US', '<h2><strong>Why does the error occur?</strong></h2>\n<p>Recently, many players from Russia have encountered problems connecting to Rust servers - the game either freezes at the \"Downloading World 0.0%\" stage</strong>, or crashes with the error \"Couldn\'t level rust\"</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>The main reason:</strong><br>Roskomnadzor blocked some of Cloudflare\'s IP addresses, which are used by Rust servers to check licenses and download data. Because of this, the game cannot connect to the server, and the download process is interrupted.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr>\n<h2><strong>How to solve the problem?</strong></h2>\n<h3><strong>1. Using VPN</strong></h3>\n<p>The easiest way to bypass the blocking is to turn on VPN</strong>&nbsp;before launching Rust. Any working services will do:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Windscribe</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>ProtonVPN</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Mullvad</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>WireGuard</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>?&nbsp;<strong>Important:</strong>&nbsp;After connecting to the VPN, restart Steam and try to log in to the server again.</p>\n<h3><strong>2. Alternative DNS</strong></h3>\n<p>Sometimes changing DNS to<strong>Google (8.8.8.8 / 8.8.4.4)</strong> or<strong>Cloudflare (1.1.1.1)</strong> helps.</p>\n<h3><strong>3. Play on our servers!</strong></h3>\n<p>If you don\'t want to mess around with VPN, join<strong>our servers</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; we have a stable connection, low ping and no problems with blocking!</p>\n<p>?&nbsp;<strong>IP of our servers</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr>\n<h2><strong>Additional solutions if Rust does not start (EAC errors)</strong></h2>\n<p>If the game crashes with an error&nbsp;<strong>EasyAntiCheat (EAC)</strong>, try the following methods:</p>\n<h3><strong>1. Checking game files via Steam</strong></h3>\n<ol start=\"1\">\n<li>\n<p>Open Steam &rarr; Library &rarr; RMB on Rust &rarr;&nbsp;<strong>Properties</strong>&nbsp;&rarr;&nbsp;<strong>Verify integrity of files</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Wait until the check is complete and restart the game.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3><strong>2. Manual EAC repair</strong></h3>\n<ol start=\"1\">\n<li>\n<p>Go to the Rust folder:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>RMB on Rust in Steam &rarr; Controls &rarr; View local files</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Open the&nbsp;<strong>EasyAntiCheat</strong></p> folder\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>In the Explorer address bar, enter:</p>\n<div class=\"md-code-block\">\n<div class=\"md-code-block-banner-wrap\">\n<div class=\"md-code-block-banner\">\n<div class=\"md-code-block-infostring\">&nbsp;</div>\n<div class=\"md-code-block-action\">\n<div class=\"ds-markdown-code-copy-button\">Copy</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<pre>EasyAntiCheat_EOS_Setup.exe repair</pre>\n</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Confirm run as administrator.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3><strong>3. Deleting the RustClient.exe.eac file</strong></h3>\n<ol start=\"1\">\n<li>\n<p>Go to the&nbsp;<strong>EasyAntiCheat</strong>&nbsp; folder (as indicated above).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Find the&nbsp;<strong>RustClient.exe.eac</strong>&nbsp; file and delete it.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Restart the game.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3><strong>4. Checking antivirus and firewall</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Temporarily disable antivirus (Avast, Kaspersky, etc.).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Add Rust and Steam to firewall exceptions.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><strong>5. Complete reinstallation of Rust</strong></h3>\n<p>If nothing helped, do a&nbsp;<strong>clean reinstallation</strong>:</p>\n<ol start=\"1\">\n<li>\n<p>Uninstall Rust via Steam.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Manually delete the&nbsp;<code>Rust</code>&nbsp;folder in&nbsp;<code>Steam\\steamapps\\common\\</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Reinstall the game.<br><br></p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2><strong>Conclusion</strong></h2>\n<p>If Rust does not connect to the server due to&nbsp;<strong>\"Downloading World 0.0%\"</strong>&nbsp;&mdash; the problem is Cloudflare blocking.&nbsp;<strong>VPN or our server</strong>&nbsp;will solve it.<br>If the game crashes because of&nbsp;<strong>EAC</strong> &mdash;try the methods above.</p>'),
(18129, 'en-US', '<h2><strong>Why does EAC block Bloody and A4Tech mice?</strong></h2>\n<p>Since December 11, 2019, the Rust anti-cheat (EasyAntiCheat) has started blocking mice of the Bloody and A4Tech brands. The reason is These devices are often used&nbsp;<strong>for macros</strong> that compensate for recoil, giving an unfair advantage in combat.</p>\n<p>If you have such a mouse connected, the game&nbsp;<strong>will not start</strong>, and instead a message will appear:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>\"EAC: Blacklisted device - Bloody Mouse\"<br></strong></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr>\n<h2><strong>How to fix the error?</strong></h2>\n<h3><strong>1. Disconnect the banned mouse</strong></h3>\n<ol start=\"1\">\n<li>\n<p>Close Rust completely.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Disconnect the Bloody/A4Tech mouse</strong>&nbsp;from the computer.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Connect&nbsp;<strong>another mouse</strong>&nbsp;(Razer, Logitech, SteelSeries, etc.).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Run Rust &mdash; the error should disappear.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h3><strong>2. Which mice are banned?</strong></h3>\n<p>EAC blocks&nbsp;<strong>only</strong>&nbsp;devices of these brands:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Bloody</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>A4Tech</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>✅&nbsp;<strong>Allowed brands</strong>&nbsp;(work without problems):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Razer</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Logitech</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Corsair</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>SteelSeries</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Zowie</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>HyperX</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>ASUS</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>and others.<br><br></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2><strong>Is it possible to play with a Bloody/A4Tech mouse?</strong></h2>\n<p><strong>On official servers &mdash; no.</strong>&nbsp;EAC strictly blocks these devices, and there is no way to bypass this<strong>without replacing the mouse</strong>&nbsp;.</p>\n<h3><strong>But there is good news!</strong></h3>\n<p><strong>On our servers, we allow any mice</strong>, including Bloody and A4Tech. We don\'t have any strict restrictions, so you can:<br>✔ Play with any mouse</strong>&nbsp;without blocking.<br>✔ Don\'t worry about&nbsp;<strong>false anti-cheat alarms</strong>.<br>✔ Enjoy stable gameplay&nbsp;<strong>without crashes</strong>.</p>\n<p>?&nbsp;<strong>Join us!</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<hr>\n<h2><strong>Conclusion</strong></h2>\n<p>If Rust doesn\'t start because of&nbsp;<strong>\"EAC: Blacklisted device\"</strong>, just change your mouse to an allowed one. But if you don\'t want to give up your device &mdash; welcome&nbsp;<strong>to our servers</strong>, where you can play without limits!</p>\n<p>?&nbsp;<strong>Any questions left?</strong> Write in the comments or visit our Discord!</p>'),
