(18148, 'en-US', '<h2>Why does the error occur?</h2><p> Recently, many players from Russia have encountered a problem when connecting to Rust servers - the game either freezes at the <strong>\"Downloading World 0.0%\"</strong> stage, or crashes with the error <strong>\"Couldn\'t level rust\"</strong> .</p><p> <strong>Main reason:</strong><br> Roskomnadzor has blocked some of Cloudflare\'s IP addresses used by Rust servers. Because of this, the game cannot connect to the server.</p><br/><h2> How to solve the problem?</h2><h3> 1. Using VPN</h3><p> The easiest way to bypass the block is <strong>to enable VPN</strong> before running Rust:</p><ul><li> Windscribe</li><li> ProtonVPN</li><li> Mullvad</li><li> WireGuard</li></ul><p> ? <strong>Important:</strong> After connecting to the VPN, restart Steam.</p><h3> 2. Alternative DNS</h3><p> Try changing DNS to:</p><ul><li> Google (8.8.8.8 / 8.8.4.4)</li><li> Cloudflare (1.1.1.1)</li></ul><h3> 3. Play on our servers!</h3><p> Join <strong>our servers</strong> - stable connection and low ping.</p><p> ? <strong>IP of our servers</strong></p><br/><h2> Additional solutions (if Rust does not start)</h2><h3> 1. Checking game files</h3><ol><li> Steam → Library → RMB on Rust → Properties → Check file integrity</li><li> Wait for the verification to complete</li></ol><h3> 2. Manual repair of EAC</h3><ol><li> Go to the Rust folder via Steam</li><li> Open the EasyAntiCheat folder</li><li> Run: <code>EasyAntiCheat_EOS_Setup.exe repair</code></li></ol><h3> 3. Deleting the RustClient.exe.eac file</h3><ol><li> In the EasyAntiCheat folder, find and delete RustClient.exe.eac</li><li> Restart the game</li></ol><h3> 4. Antivirus check</h3><ul><li> Temporarily disable your antivirus</li><li> Add Rust to exceptions</li></ul><h3> 5. Complete reinstallation</h3><ol><li> Uninstall Rust via Steam</li><li> Delete the Rust folder manually</li><li> Reinstall the game</li></ol><br/><h2> Conclusion</h2><p> If the problem is <strong>\"Downloading World 0.0%\"</strong> - use VPN or our server.<br> If there are EAC errors, try the methods above.</p>'),
(18149, 'en-US', 'EAC: Blacklisted device - Bloody Mouse - how to play with banned mice?'),
(18150, 'en-US', '<p>If Rust gives the error <strong>\"EAC: Blacklisted device - Bloody Mouse\"</strong> , it means that your mouse is blocked due to suspicion of cheating. In this article, we will analyze which devices are prohibited, how to bypass the blocking and on which servers you can play with any mouse without problems.</p>'),
(18151, 'en-US', '<h2><strong>Why does EAC block Bloody and A4Tech mice?</strong></h2><p> Since <strong>December 11, 2019,</strong> the Rust anti-cheat (EasyAntiCheat) has started blocking mice of <strong>the Bloody and A4Tech</strong> brands. The reason is that these devices are often used <strong>for macros</strong> that compensate for recoil, giving an unfair advantage in combat.</p><p> If you have such a mouse connected, the game <strong>will not start</strong> , and instead the following message will appear:</p><blockquote><p> <strong>\"EAC: Blacklisted device - Bloody Mouse\"<br></strong></p></blockquote><p></p><hr><h2> <strong>How to fix the error?</strong></h2><h3> <strong>1. Disable the prohibited mouse</strong></h3><ol start=\"1\"><li><p> Close Rust completely.</p></li><li><p> <strong>Disconnect the Bloody/A4Tech mouse</strong> from the computer.</p></li><li><p> Connect <strong>another mouse</strong> (Razer, Logitech, SteelSeries, etc.).</p></li><li><p> Run Rust and the error should disappear.</p></li></ol><h3> <strong>2. What mice are prohibited?</strong></h3><p> EAC <strong>only</strong> blocks devices from these brands:</p><ul><li><p> <strong>Bloody</strong></p></li><li><p> <strong>A4Tech</strong></p></li></ul><p> ✅ <strong>Approved brands</strong> (work without problems):</p><ul><li><p> Razer</p></li><li><p> Logitech</p></li><li><p> Corsair</p></li><li><p> SteelSeries</p></li><li><p> Zowie</p></li><li><p> HyperX</p></li><li><p> ASUS</p></li><li><p> and others.<br><br></p></li></ul><hr><h2> <strong>Is it possible to play Bloody/A4Tech with a mouse?</strong></h2><p> <strong>On official servers - no.</strong> EAC strictly blocks these devices, and there is no way to bypass this <strong>without replacing the mouse</strong> .</p><h3> <strong>But there is good news!</strong></h3><p> <strong>On our servers we allow any mouse</strong> , including Bloody and A4Tech. We don\'t have any hard restrictions, so you can:<br> ✔ Play <strong>with any mouse</strong> without blocking.<br> ✔ Don\'t worry about <strong>false positives from anti-cheat</strong> .<br> ✔ Enjoy stable gameplay <strong>without crashes</strong> .</p><p> ? <strong>Join us!</strong></p><p></p><hr><h2> <strong>Conclusion</strong></h2><p> If Rust doesn\'t launch because of <strong>\"EAC: Blacklisted device\"</strong> , just change your mouse to an allowed one. But if you don\'t want to give up your device - welcome <strong>to our servers</strong> , where you can play without restrictions!</p><p> ? <strong>Any questions left?</strong> Write in the comments or visit our Discord!</p>'),
(18152, 'en-US', 'Why Rust Can\'t Find Servers? Solving the Server Display Problem'),
(18153, 'en-US', '<p>If Rust does not see servers, shows only modified ones or freezes when loading a world, this may be due to blocking, cache settings or network problems. In this article, we will analyze how to fix the error and how to play on our servers without these problems.</p>'),
(18154, 'en-US', '<h2><strong>Why doesn\'t Rust show servers?</strong></h2><p> Players often encounter problems like these:</p><ul><li><p> <strong>Servers are not displayed</strong> (only 30-50 out of 2000+ are visible)</p></li><li><p> <strong>Official servers are gone</strong> , but mods and \"Favorites\" are working</p></li><li><p> <strong>Stuck on loading world</strong> (0.0% or 15%)</p></li><li><p> <strong>Error \"Wrong Connection Protocol\"</strong></p></li></ul><h3> <strong>Main reasons:</strong></h3><ol start=\"1\"><li><p> <strong>Blocking IP addresses</strong> (especially in Crimea and some regions of the Russian Federation)</p></li><li><p> <strong>Steam Server Cache Issues</strong></p></li><li><p> <strong>Network or antivirus errors</strong> (even if it is \"disabled\")</p></li><li><p> <strong>Outdated version of the game</strong></p></li></ol><hr><h2> <strong>How to fix the problem?</strong></h2><h3> <strong>1. Disable server caching</strong></h3><ol start=\"1\"><li><p> In the Rust Servers menu, click <strong>\"Filters\"</strong> .</p></li><li><p> <strong>Uncheck the box</strong> next to <em>\"Use server cache\"</em> .</p></li><li><p> Click <strong>\"Update\"</strong> .</p></li></ol><p> ? <em>This method helps if only modified servers are visible.</em></p><h3> <strong>2. Check your internet connection</strong></h3><ul><li><p> <strong>Reboot your router</strong> (turn it off for 1 minute).</p></li><li><p> <strong>Try VPN</strong> (if the problem is IP blocking).</p></li><li><p> <strong>Check DNS</strong> (use Google DNS <code>8.8.8.8</code> / <code>8.8.4.4</code> ).</p></li></ul><h3> <strong>3. Check the integrity of the game files</strong></h3><ol start=\"1\"><li><p> In Steam: <strong>Library → RMB on Rust → Properties → Verify integrity of files</strong> .</p></li><li><p> Wait until it completes and restart the game.</p></li></ol><h3> <strong>4. Disable User Account Control (UAC)</strong></h3><ol start=\"1\"><li><p> Press <strong>Win + R</strong> , enter <code>msconfig</code> → <strong>OK</strong> .</p></li><li><p> Go to the <strong>\"Tools\"</strong> tab → find <strong>\"Change User Account Control settings\"</strong> .</p></li><li><p> Move the slider down ( <strong>Never notify</strong> ) → <strong>OK</strong> .</p></li><li><p> <strong>Restart your PC</strong> .</p></li></ol><h3> <strong>5. Connect via IP manually</strong></h3><p> If the servers are not displayed, try to go <strong>directly by IP</strong> :</p><ol start=\"1\"><li><p> From the Rust main menu, press <strong>F1</strong> .</p></li><li><p> Enter: </p><div class=\"md-code-block\"><div class=\"md-code-block-banner-wrap\"><div class=\"md-code-block-banner\"><div class=\"md-code-block-infostring\"></div><div class=\"md-code-block-action\"><div class=\"ds-markdown-code-copy-button\"> Copy</div></div></div></div><pre> client.connect 195.18.27.169:35100</pre></div><p> (replace with the IP of the desired server).</p></li></ol><hr><h2> <strong>Why is it worth playing on our servers?</strong></h2><p> If the official servers are down, we have <strong>a stable connection without blocking</strong> :<br> ✅ <strong>No problems with displaying servers</strong><br> ✅ <strong>No freezes on loading the world</strong><br> ✅ <strong>Active community and protection from cheaters</strong></p><p> ? <strong>Join us!</strong><br> Server IP: connect 195.18.27.169:35100</p><hr><h2> <strong>Conclusion</strong></h2><p> If Rust doesn\'t see the server, try <strong>disabling the cache, checking DNS or using a VPN</strong> . If you don\'t want to waste time on settings, visit <strong>us</strong> where everything works without problems!</p><p> ? <strong>Any questions left?</strong> Write in the comments or in our Discord!</p>'),
(18155, 'en-US', 'Error \"Failed to validate premium status: Network Err\" in Rust - how to fix?'),
(18156, 'en-US', '<p>If you see the error <strong>\"Failed to validate premium status: Network Err\"</strong> when entering the Rust premium server, it means that the game cannot verify your \"premium status\". In this article, we will analyze the reasons and solutions, and also tell you how to play on our servers without these restrictions.</p>'),
(18157, 'en-US', '<h2><strong>Why does this error appear?</strong></h2><p> With <strong>the latest update,</strong> Rust introduced the <strong>Premium Servers</strong> system - special servers available only to players who have Rust skins worth <strong>$15 or more</strong> in their Steam inventory.</p><h3> <strong>The main reasons for the error:</strong></h3><ol start=\"1\"><li><p> <strong>You don\'t have any skins worth $15+ in your inventory</strong> (or their value has dropped).</p></li><li><p> <strong>Steam sync issues</strong> (new purchases may take up to 20 minutes to update).</p></li><li><p> <strong>Network failures</strong> (Steam was unable to verify your status).</p></li><li><p> <strong>Using VPN</strong> (may interfere with verification).<br><br></p></li></ol><hr><h2> <strong>How to fix the error?</strong></h2><h3> <strong>1. Check if you have a premium status</strong></h3><ol start=\"1\"><li><p> Open <strong>your Steam inventory</strong> ( <a href=\"https://steamcommunity.com/id/me/inventory/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">link</a> ).</p></li><li><p> Select <strong>Rust</strong> and calculate the total cost of the skins (should be <strong>$15+</strong> ).</p><ul><li><p> <strong>The following are taken into account:</strong> weapon skins, buildings, decorations.</p></li><li><p> <strong>Not included:</strong> DLC (musical instruments, Voice Props, etc.).</p></li></ul></li></ol><h3> <strong>2. If there are not enough skins</strong></h3><ul><li><p> <strong>Buy skins</strong> from the Steam Market (for example, cheap <strong>\"Wooden Door\"</strong> or <strong>\"Large Box\"</strong> ).</p></li><li><p> <strong>Please wait 20 minutes</strong> - Steam may be delayed in updating your status.</p></li></ul><h3> <strong>3. Update the status manually</strong></h3><ol start=\"1\"><li><p> In the Rust server menu, click on <strong>the Premium icon</strong> .</p></li><li><p> Click on <strong>\"Refresh\"</strong> (circle arrow).</p></li></ol><h3> <strong>4. Check your internet connection</strong></h3><ul><li><p> <strong>Disable VPN</strong> (if using).</p></li><li><p> <strong>Restart Steam</strong> and Rust.</p></li></ul><hr><h2> <strong>Alternative: play on our servers!</strong></h2><p> If you don\'t want to spend money on skins, <strong>we have no restrictions on Premium status</strong> . Our servers are available <strong>to all players</strong> , without inventory checks!</p><p> ✅ <strong>No \"Failed to validate premium status\"</strong><br> ✅ <strong>Stable online and protection from cheaters</strong><br> ✅ <strong>Play immediately - no waiting or updates<br><br></strong></p><hr><h2> <strong>Conclusion</strong></h2><p> The <strong>\"Failed to validate premium status\"</strong> error appears if you <strong>don\'t have $15+ worth of skins</strong> on Steam. Solution:<br> ✔ <strong>Buy more skins</strong> and wait 20 minutes.<br> ✔ <strong>Update the status</strong> in the server menu.<br> ✔ <strong>Play with us</strong> - without unnecessary restrictions!</p><p> ? <strong>Any questions left?</strong> Write in the comments or visit our Discord!</p>'),
