(18283, 'en-US', 'Wipe on all servers SIMPLE RUST'),
(18284, 'en-US', 'Wipe on all our servers! Hurry up to join the wipe!'),
(18285, 'en-US', '<h2>? THIS FRIDAY WIPE ON ALL OUR SERVERS!</h2><ul> ⁠<li> ? July 18 at 16:00 Moscow time</li><li> ? Only players who have played on our servers for more than 1 hour can vote for the map!</li><li> ? There will be a GLOBAL WIPE on servers X2-[weekly] and MAX4-X2!</li></ul><h2> Don\'t forget to vote for the maps:</h2><ul><li> <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/maps/max3\">「⏩」MAX3</a></li><li> <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/maps/classicx2\">「⏩」X2-[weekly]</a></li><li> <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/maps/nolimit\">「⏩」NOLIMIT</a></li><li> <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/maps/max8\">「⏩」MAX8</a></li><li> <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/maps/classic14x2\">「⏩」X2-[2 weeks]</a></li><li> <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/maps/max4x2\">「⏩」MAX4-X2</a></li><li> <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/servers/x10\">「⏩」VANILLA-X10</a></li></ul>'),
(18286, 'en-US', 'How to loot Cosmodrome Rust'),
(18287, 'en-US', 'Guide to looting RT Cosmodrome plant.'),
(18288, 'en-US', '<p>Entrance to the metro at the cosmodrome </p><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/y1bNbwj/photo-2025-07-17-20-42-56.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-20-42-56\" border=\"0\"></p><h2> ? Launcher</h2><p> The launch pad is an open area with massive underground rooms and a huge rocket in the center. There are two main points with valuable loot and several additional, smaller ones. In total, up to 15 containers can be found in this part of the spaceport, but most of them are ordinary wooden boxes.</p><h3> ? Main loot points</h3><ul><li> <strong>Underground complex:</strong> high-grade boxes, but hard to reach - requires running a considerable distance and showing agility.</li><li> <strong>Central Metal Structure:</strong> A huge structure with two elevators; easy to get to the loot if you know the route.</li><li> <strong>Small kennels:</strong> simple boxes, easy access.</li></ul><h3> ? Looting route on the launcher</h3><h4> ? Step 1: Wooden booths</h4><ul><li> Enter through the central entrance.</li><li> Loot the first booth (1 box).</li><li> In the second booth there is a lever: red - activate, green - leave.</li><li> At the overturned truck, turn right and find the third booth with a box.</li></ul><h4> ? Step 2: Underground tunnels</h4><p> Behind the third booth is a concrete tunnel. Inside, the second lever is activated. Along the way, you can collect boxes and break barrels. Be careful - there is a tank driving on the surface.</p><h4> ? Step 3: The lower part of the metal structure</h4><p> Carefully get to the central area. Jump onto the railing, then onto the metal side. Walk along the beam after activating the timer. Inside there are up to 5 chests.</p><h4> ? Step 4: Top of the metal structure</h4><p> We go up the stairs and the elevator. It is best to go up and down, looting the platforms. It is safer to jump on the railings. If you have medicine, you can jump on the platforms themselves. </p><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/NgQKpgdN/photo-2025-07-17-20-43-32.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-20-43-32\" border=\"0\"></p><hr><h2> ? Office area</h2><p> To safely explore the offices you will need:</p><ul><li> ? Medicines</li><li> ? Anti-radiation pills</li><li> ? Anti-radiation suit</li><li> ? Green, ? blue and ? red cards </li></ul><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/fY1dqpQs/photo-2025-07-17-20-43-37.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-20-43-37\" border=\"0\"></p><h3> ? Where to find the necessary items?</h3><ul><li> <strong>Fuses:</strong> Drop randomly from crates and barrels.</li><li> <strong>Green Card:</strong> Found on NPCs and in crates.</li><li> <strong>Blue card:</strong> lies in rooms opened by the green one.</li><li> <strong>Red Card:</strong> Found in areas accessible via the Blue Card.</li></ul><h3> ? Office looting stages</h3><h4> ? Step 1: Warehouses and utility rooms</h4><p> It\'s better to approach from the rear. Insert the fuse into the building at the left corner and activate the lever. </p><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/TxyRGNtR/photo-2025-07-17-20-43-46.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-20-43-46\" border=\"0\"></p><h4> ? Step 2: Building with army crate</h4><p> Go around the building, climb the pallets and the canopy, jump over the fence. Inside is an army box. </p><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/FLpbrfzb/photo-2025-07-17-20-44-04.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-20-44-04\" border=\"0\"></p><h4> ? Step 3: Main Office</h4><p> Insert the second fuse, open the door with the red card. There are valuable boxes hidden on each floor. There is an elite container on the roof. <img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/dwgrQnWr/photo-2025-07-17-20-44-10.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-20-44-10\" border=\"0\"></p><hr><h2> ? Puzzle Solution</h2><ul><li> You will need: ? green card, ? red card, 2 ⚙️ fuses.</li><li> The first building is at the loading area, next to the trucks. Insert the fuse and activate the lever. </li></ul><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/Kzspj31j/photo-2025-07-17-20-44-14.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-20-44-14\" border=\"0\"></p><ol> Entrance to the fuse holder </ol><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/4Z5ZwYWz/photo-2025-07-17-20-44-22.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-20-44-22\" border=\"0\"></p><ul><li> The second building is near three tanks. On the first floor, insert the fuse and turn on the power. </li></ul><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/KpZjX7BK/photo-2025-07-17-21-29-45.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-21-29-45\" border=\"0\"></p><p> The second building where the fuse holder is located </p><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/ynC4KRBK/photo-2025-07-17-21-31-13.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-21-31-13\" border=\"0\"></p><p> Fuse holder in the second building</p><ul><li> Now we go to the main building. Any of the 4 entrances can be opened with a red card. </li></ul><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/kVXq9rGd/photo-2025-07-17-20-44-35.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-20-44-35\" border=\"0\"></p><p> One of the entrances to the main building </p><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/4RkMS2dp/photo-2025-07-17-20-44-39.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-20-44-39\" border=\"0\"></p><p> View of the main building inside </p><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/d48zYyDr/photo-2025-07-17-20-44-44.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-20-44-44\" border=\"0\"></p><p> Roof of the rocket factory</p><hr><h2> ? Equipment for the spaceport</h2><ul><li> <strong>For jogging:</strong> burlap and light armor.</li><li> <strong>For full looting:</strong> anti-radiation suit. </li></ul><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/yzM9PXg/photo-2025-07-17-21-46-10.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-21-46-10\" border=\"0\"></p><hr><h2> ?‍? Enemies on the territory</h2><p> There are 8 scientists inside the main building:</p><ul><li> 2 - at the lower level</li><li> 2 - on the roof</li><li> The rest are on intermediate platforms</li><li> And don\'t forget that there is a tank driving around the cosmodrome!</li></ul><h2> ?‍ View from above </h2><p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/pBqByqb1/photo-2025-07-17-21-55-33.jpg\" alt=\"photo-2025-07-17-21-55-33\" border=\"0\"></p><p> To the left of the entrance to the industrial zone, between two warehouses, there is a recycler, and to the right, on the second floor of one of the offices, there is a study table. Next to the table, you will also find a repair workbench. Be careful when using them: other players often set up ambushes near points of interest.</p><p></p><p></p>'),
(18289, 'en-US', 'Average neon that glare!'),
(18290, 'en-US', 'Switch I'),
(18291, 'en-US', 'OR switch'),
(18292, 'en-US', 'XOR switch'),
(18293, 'en-US', 'Access to the <strong><span style=\"color: #aaf16e;\">/skin</span></strong> command which allows you to easily and quickly change the skins you add <a href=\"/custom-skins\" target=\"_blank\">in this section</a> .'),
(18294, 'en-US', 'A Second Chance for Metal Detectors in Rust - Now Loot Won\'t Go into the Sand Forever'),
(18295, 'en-US', 'Now loot in Rust does not disappear, but is buried in the ground - you can get it with a metal detector. Returning your favorite Kalashnikov is now possible!'),
(18296, 'en-US', '<section><h2>? Metal detectors are back in the game with a vengeance</h2><p> For a long time, <strong>metal detectors</strong> in Rust were more like a souvenir: an interesting, but not very useful thing. However, times are changing - the developers decided to breathe a second life into them.</p></section><section><h2> ? Loot goes underground, not into oblivion</h2><p> According to the latest changes, <strong>weapons and backpacks</strong> will no longer simply <em>disspawn</em> after battles. Instead, they will **bury themselves in the ground** at the location where the player dies.</p><p> This means that now you can <strong>find hidden goods with a metal detector</strong> . Not just wander along the beach looking for nails, but actually dig up what was yesterday your favorite Kalashnikov!</p></section><section><h2> ? What does this change?</h2><p> Players now have a chance <strong>to get back lost loot</strong> if they manage to return and use the metal detector correctly. Perhaps even ambushes will become more cunning - the enemy thinks you\'ve left, and you\'re digging right under his nose ?</p></section>'),
(18297, 'en-US', 'Rust DLC — Full Guide: What They Are, What They Give, Where to Buy, and How to Save'),
(18298, 'en-US', 'Full list of Rust DLCs: what\'s included in each pack - from barrels and jungles to musical instruments. We tell you in detail about each Rust DLC, what it looks like and why you need it. Where to buy and how to save money.'),
(18299, 'en-US', '<p>DLC (Downloadable Content) are extensions to Rust that add unique items, styles, musical instruments, voice capabilities, and even change the visual appearance of buildings. Below, we have collected a complete description of all available DLC for 2025.</p><h2> ? Quick links</h2><ul><li> <a href=\"#jungle\">Jungle Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#frontier\">Frontier Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#sunburn\">Sunburn Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#arctic\">Arctic Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#instrument\">Instrument Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#voice\">Voice Props</a></li><li> <a href=\"#ancient\">Ancient Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#abyss\">Abyss Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#pilot\">Pilot Pack</a></li></ul><hr><h2 id=\"jungle\"> ? Jungle Pack DLC </h2><p><img src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/jungle-pack-og.jpg\" alt=\"Jungle Pack DLC\"></p><p> Give your base a tropical makeover with jungle-inspired furniture, decor, and textures.</p><ul><li> Palm bed</li><li> Bamboo chairs and tables</li><li> Wall Mask Reptile</li><li> Wooden Totem Torches</li></ul><h2 id=\"frontier\"> ? Frontier Pack DLC </h2><p><img src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/rust_frontiersman_hero_02.jpg\" alt=\"Frontier Pack DLC\"></p><p> DLC with barrels is one of the most useful sets for PvE and RP bases. Stylized as \"Wild West\".</p><ul><li> <strong>Barrel Storage</strong> - a large storage unit (like a large box)</li><li> Saloon Door - Double Cowboy Door</li><li> Chandelier, wooden furniture, gun rack</li></ul><h2 id=\"sunburn\"> ? Sunburn Pack DLC</h2><p><img src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/sunburn-header.jpg\" alt=\"Sunburn Pack DLC\"></p><p> Summer aesthetic: beach vacation at your own base. Pairs well with RP.</p><ul><li> Inflatable pool</li><li> Sun loungers, umbrellas</li><li> Towel (spawnpoint)</li><li> Clothing - glasses, t-shirts, bathing suits</li></ul><h2 id=\"arctic\"> ❄ Arctic Pack DLC</h2><p><img src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/iceassaultrifle.jpg\" alt=\"Arctic Pack DLC\"></p><p> DLC for snow biomes. Items look like expedition gear.</p><ul><li> Arctic Hazmat Suit</li><li> Fur hoods, wraps</li><li> Snow camouflage</li></ul><h2 id=\"instrument\"> ? Instrument Pack DLC </h2><p><img src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/ss_383b5d3c204dd6fd7dc6eac1643f14de35293363.1920x1080.jpg\" alt=\"Instrument Pack DLC\"></p><p> The first music DLC in Rust. Allows you to play instruments manually or with a MIDI keyboard.</p><ul><li> Guitar, bass guitar</li><li> Xylophone, keys, drums</li><li> Trumpet, saxophone</li><li> Bongo, pots</li></ul><h2 id=\"voice\"> ? Voice Props DLC </h2><p><img src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/Rust-Voice-Props-DLC-803x452.jpg\" alt=\"Voice Props DLC\"></p><p> An audio supplement for lovers of creativity and atmosphere.</p><ul><li> Speakers (sound reproduction)</li><li> Cassette recorder and cassettes</li><li> Radio and voice amplifiers</li><li> Microphones, disco lights</li></ul><h2 id=\"ancient\"> ? Ancient Pack DLC </h2><p><img src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/cDjTrmjWNic3QEmhkeWuLQ.jpg\" alt=\"Ancient Pack DLC\"></p><p> Stylization of ancient civilizations: columns, stone patterns, tarnished metal.</p><ul><li> Stone walls with symbols</li><li> Clay and bronze elements</li><li> Torches and columns</li></ul><h2 id=\"abyss\"> ? Abyss Pack DLC </h2><p><img src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/F0X0GjYaQAAl9MG.jpg\" alt=\"Abyss Pack DLC\"></p><p> Underwater theme. Great for ocean bases and deep caves.</p><ul><li> Helmet with backlight</li><li> Dark suits with steel accents</li><li> Decorations for underwater buildings</li></ul><hr><h2> ? Where to buy DLC Rust?</h2><ul><li> <strong>Steam</strong> - all official DLCs are sold on the game page.</li><li> <strong>Rust DLC Bundle</strong> - sometimes available during sales.</li><li> <strong>FunPay</strong> - accounts with already activated DLC (unofficial).</li></ul><h2> ? Buying tips</h2><ol><li> Expect seasonal discounts (summer, autumn, winter, spring).</li><li> Buy DLCs as a set.</li><li> Do not use DLC Unlocker - it violates Steam rules and may result in a ban.</li></ol><h2> ✅ Conclusion</h2><p> The most useful DLCs are <strong>Frontier (barrels)</strong> , <strong>Arctic (cold protection)</strong> , <strong>Instrument</strong> and <strong>Voice Props</strong> for creativity. The rest are for atmosphere and base customization. Choose based on your playstyle!</p>'),
