c\"> ❄ Arctic Pack DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/iceassaultrifle.jpg\" alt=\"Arctic Pack DLC\"></p><p> DLC for snow biomes. Items look like expedition gear.</p><ul><li> Arctic Hazmat Suit</li><li> Fur hoods, wraps</li><li> Snow camouflage</li></ul><h2 id=\"instrument\"> ? Instrument Pack DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/ss_383b5d3c204dd6fd7dc6eac1643f14de35293363.1920x1080.jpg\" alt=\"Instrument Pack DLC\"></p><p> The first music DLC in Rust. Allows you to play instruments manually or with a MIDI keyboard.</p><ul><li> Guitar, bass guitar</li><li> Xylophone, keys, drums</li><li> Trumpet, saxophone</li><li> Bongo, pots</li></ul><h2 id=\"voice\"> ? Voice Props DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/Rust-Voice-Props-DLC-803x452.jpg\" alt=\"Voice Props DLC\"></p><p> An audio supplement for lovers of creativity and atmosphere.</p><ul><li> Speakers (sound reproduction)</li><li> Cassette recorder and cassettes</li><li> Radio and voice amplifiers</li><li> Microphones, disco lights</li></ul><h2 id=\"ancient\"> ? Ancient Pack DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/cDjTrmjWNic3QEmhkeWuLQ.jpg\" alt=\"Ancient Pack DLC\"></p><p> Stylization of ancient civilizations: columns, stone patterns, tarnished metal.</p><ul><li> Stone walls with symbols</li><li> Clay and bronze elements</li><li> Torches and columns</li></ul><h2 id=\"abyss\"> ? Abyss Pack DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/F0X0GjYaQAAl9MG.jpg\" alt=\"Abyss Pack DLC\"></p><p> Underwater theme. Great for ocean bases and deep caves.</p><ul><li> Helmet with backlight</li><li> Dark suits with steel accents</li><li> Decorations for underwater buildings</li></ul><hr><h2> ? Where to buy DLC Rust?</h2><ul><li> <strong>Steam</strong> - all official DLCs are sold on the game page.</li><li> <strong>Rust DLC Bundle</strong> - sometimes available during sales.</li><li> <strong>FunPay</strong> - accounts with already activated DLC (unofficial).</li></ul><h2> ? Buying tips</h2><ol><li> Expect seasonal discounts (summer, autumn, winter, spring).</li><li> Buy DLCs as a set.</li><li> Do not use DLC Unlocker - it violates Steam rules and may result in a ban.</li></ol><h2> ✅ Conclusion</h2><p> The most useful DLCs are <strong>Frontier (barrels)</strong> , <strong>Arctic (cold protection)</strong> , <strong>Instrument</strong> and <strong>Voice Props</strong> for creativity. The rest are for atmosphere and base customization. Choose based on your playstyle!</p>'),
(18302, 'en-US', 'Cheats on Rust - why is it a path to ban | The dangers of cheats and account bans');
INSERT INTO `language_translate` (`id`, `language`, `translation`) VALUES
(18303, 'en-US', 'Looking for Rust cheats? Find out why using them is a risk of being banned on all servers, including official and Simple. Examples of checks, private cheats and how to easily get into the cheater database.'),
(18304, 'en-US', '<p><strong>Rust cheats</strong> and <strong>cheat codes</strong> are actively sought by thousands of players: <em>rust cheats</em> - 3,769 requests per month, <em>download cheat for Rust</em> - 288. However, there is a real trap behind these numbers.</p><h2> ? Cheat on Rust - the path to ban</h2><p> You can find dozens of links offering <strong>to download Rust cheats for free</strong> or even buy <strong>a private cheat</strong> (for example, <em>Alkad, Magix, Trinity, Bummer, Superiority,</em> etc.).</p><p> But the truth is that once you install such <em>a cheat for Rust</em> , consider your account lost.</p><ul><li> <strong>EAC (Easy Anti-Cheat)</strong> works around the clock and automatically catches third-party interference in the client.</li><li> <strong>Simple Rust servers</strong> (for example, <em>Prostoj</em> , <em>Moscow77</em> ) use <strong>additional monitoring systems</strong> , detecting even private and injected cheats - <em>dll, dma, esp</em> .</li><li> Out of 15 random checks on the server, <strong>at least 1 cheater is almost always identified</strong> and sent to a lifetime ban.</li><li> Once detected, your <strong>Steam account is added to the global cheater database</strong> (including Community Ban, Devblog Tracking and VAC), and you will no longer be able to play safely on official and many custom servers.</li></ul><h2> ? Rust cheats = killed account and reputation</h2><p> Many newbies are looking for <em>a free Rust cheat</em> or <em>Rust cheats for pirates</em> ( <em>pirated Rust cheat</em> , <em>Rust ME cheat</em> , <em>old Rust cheat</em> and even <em>Rust cheats on the phone</em> ). But even on pirated versions, servers use anti-cheat plugins, and a ban there is also irreversible.</p><p> <strong>Important:</strong> Attempting to bypass anti-cheat or use injectors ( <em>Oxide, DLL-injector, memez external</em> ) results in an automatic report being sent to EAC.</p><h2> ⚠️ Rust devblog and \"exposed\" cheats</h2><p> There are dozens of links online to supposedly safe cheats for <strong>Rust devblog</strong> versions 198, 236, 240, 2590, 261 and even 292. For example:</p><ul><li> rust 2590 cheats</li><li> cheat for rust 261 devblog</li><li> superiority rust cheats 2590 download</li></ul><p> However, all these cheats are either already in the anti-cheat database, or are used as <strong>Trojans</strong> that steal Steam access.</p><h2> ? Opinion of the administration of the servers \"Simple\"</h2><blockquote> \"On our servers, a cheater does not live longer than a couple of days. We conduct end-to-end checks, save evidence, and all suspicious actions are analyzed manually and automatically. Bans are irreversible.\"</blockquote><h2> ✅ Playing fair is the real superiority</h2><p> Instead of risking your account, money, and reputation, it\'s better to level up your skills and develop. You\'ll be surprised how much fun you can have playing Rust fairly, especially on well-modded servers.</p><p> <strong>Don\'t download suspicious files, don\'t buy dubious private cheats, and don\'t look for \"magic\" cheats for old versions - all this will lead to a ban.</strong></p><hr><p> ? A safe choice is to play on <a href=\"https://prostoj.store\">Prostoj Rust</a> , where honesty is rewarded.</p>'),
(18305, 'en-US', 'Trade Protection in Rust and CS2: How it will affect skins and DLC rules'),
(18306, 'en-US', 'Valve and Facepunch are introducing Trade Protection to CS2 and Rust. Find out how your skins will now be protected, why giveaways are delayed, and what restrictions are imposed on skinboxes and DLCs.'),
(18307, 'en-US', '<p><strong>Valve</strong> has already implemented <em>Trade Protection</em> in CS2, and a similar system will be launched in <strong>Rust</strong> next week. This is an important step towards skin security and combating account hijacking.</p><h2> ? What is Trade Protection?</h2><p> Now, if your account is <strong>hacked</strong> or is seen to be involved in suspicious activity, any trade will be <strong>held for 7 days</strong> . Items will be returned to the owner, but you will receive <strong>a 30-day block on trades and the marketplace</strong> .</p><h2> ? How will this affect our giveaways?</h2><p> All skins that you win from us (for example, on <strong>Simple</strong> servers) <strong>will now also be held by the system for 7 days</strong> . This is a standard protection, do not worry - <strong>all skins will reach their owners</strong> , just with a slight delay.</p><h2> ⚠ New Facepunch Studios Rules: DLC and Skinbox Bans</h2><p> Rust developers have updated <strong>the official rules for using DLC on servers</strong> . Now:</p><ul><li> <strong>You cannot grant access to DLC</strong> unless it was purchased through Steam (e.g. via skinbox or third-party commands).</li><li> <strong>You can\'t restrict access to DLC</strong> if a player has purchased it - it should be available on any server.</li><li> <strong>You cannot bypass DLC ownership checks</strong> or fake purchases.</li></ul><p> <strong>Facepunch DLC</strong> includes official packs: <em>building skins, decor packs, hazmat, instruments, cosmetics</em> and more, sold through Steam.</p><h3> What to do now?</h3><p> <strong>Skinbox will contain less official skins</strong> , but you can <strong>add your custom skins</strong> through our section:</p><p> <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/custom-skins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://prostoj.store/custom-skins</a></p><h2> ✅ What is still possible:</h2><ul><li> Add <strong>custom skins</strong> that are not included in the official DLC.</li><li> Use <strong>Steam Workshop skins</strong> not approved by Facepunch.</li><li> Configure and restrict access to unofficial content on servers.</li></ul><hr><p> We are always monitoring and adapting to Facepunch updates to ensure you <strong>have a safe and fair experience playing on the Simple servers</strong> .</p>'),
(18308, 'en-US', 'Twitch Drops Rust - When Will They Be, Schedule, How To Get Rewards (Round 41)'),
(18309, 'en-US', 'Find out when Twitch Drops are in Rust! Full drop schedule, Round 41 (2025) reward list, FAQ, and countdown timer.'),
(18310, 'en-US', '<p>Looking for information about <strong>twitch drops in Rust</strong> ? Here you will find everything: <a href=\"#schedule\">drop schedule</a> , <a href=\"#rewards\">reward list</a> , <a href=\"#faq\">answers to frequently asked questions</a> and even <strong>the date and time of the current event</strong> .</p><hr><h2 id=\"schedule\"> ?️ When will Twitch Drops Rust be?</h2><p> Current drop event: <strong>Round 41: Global Warfare 3</strong> , hosted by FancyOrb.</p><ul><li> <strong>Launch:</strong> July 24, 2025, 20:00 Moscow time</li><li> <strong>End:</strong> August 1, 2025, 03:00 MSK</li></ul><hr><h2 id=\"rewards\"> ? What can you get? List of drops</h2><p> To earn rewards, simply watch Rust streams with the <strong>“Drops Enabled”</strong> tag on <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/drops/campaigns\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Twitch</a> .</p><ul><li> ? <strong>Wood Storage Box</strong> — 1 hour watch</li><li> ? <strong>Rug</strong> — 2 hours</li><li> ? <strong>Fridge</strong> — 3 hours</li><li> ? <strong>Sheet Metal Double Door</strong> — 4 hours</li><li> ? <strong>MP5A4</strong> - 5 hours</li><li> ⛏️ <strong>Jackhammer</strong> — 6 hours</li></ul><p> ⏩ Don\'t forget to click <strong>“Claim”</strong> on <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/drops/inventory\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the Drops Inventory page</a> , otherwise the item will not be added to your Steam.</p><hr><h2 id=\"faq\"> ❓ Frequently asked questions</h2><h3> ?<a name=\"watch\"></a> What streams to watch for drops?</h3><p> Any Rust streams with the <strong>“Drops Enabled”</strong> tag. For personal drops, go to the specific streamer’s channel.</p><h3> ?<a name=\"progress\"></a> How to track progress?</h3><p> Go to <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/drops/inventory\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">your Drops inventory</a> , you can see how much is left until the next drop.</p><h3> ? Is it possible to watch multiple streams at once to speed up?</h3><p> No. Only <strong>one active channel</strong> works - the rest are not taken into account.</p><h3> ⏱ When will the drop appear on Steam?</h3><p> Usually within 10 minutes after clicking “Claim”. If not after 30 minutes, check <strong>your Steam to Twitch link</strong> .</p><h3> ? Do you need Twitch Prime?</h3><p> No, a regular Twitch account and Rust in your Steam library are enough.</p><h3> ? How to unlink an old Twitch and link a new one?</h3><p> Go to <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/drops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the Drops page</a> on Steam, click “Unlink Account”, then connect your new Twitch.</p><h3> ? If I haven\'t bought Rust yet, will the drops be saved?</h3><p> Yes, if you <strong>managed to pick</strong> them up. They are stored for up to 180 days. After purchasing Rust, just check the binding and click “Check for Missing Drops”.</p><h3> ? What are Crates for?</h3><p> These are Steam Crates containing one random Rust item. To open:</p><ol><li> Launch the game Rust</li><li> Go to the menu - Inventory</li><li> Select Crate and click “Open”</li></ol><hr><h2 id=\"extra\"> ? Useful links</h2><ul><li> <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/drops/campaigns\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Active Twitch Drops Campaigns</a></li><li> <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/drops/inventory\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">My inventory of drops</a></li><li> <a href=\"https://www.rustafied.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Official Rust News</a></li></ul>'),
