e active channel</strong> works - the rest are not taken into account.</p><h3> ⏱ When will the drop appear on Steam?</h3><p> Usually within 10 minutes after clicking “Claim”. If not after 30 minutes, check <strong>your Steam to Twitch link</strong> .</p><h3> ? Do you need Twitch Prime?</h3><p> No, a regular Twitch account and Rust in your Steam library are enough.</p><h3> ? How to unlink an old Twitch and link a new one?</h3><p> Go to <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/drops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the Drops page</a> on Steam, click “Unlink Account”, then connect your new Twitch.</p><h3> ? If I haven\'t bought Rust yet, will the drops be saved?</h3><p> Yes, if you <strong>managed to pick</strong> them up. They are stored for up to 180 days. After purchasing Rust, just check the binding and click “Check for Missing Drops”.</p><h3> ? What are Crates for?</h3><p> These are Steam Crates containing one random Rust item. To open:</p><ol><li> Launch the game Rust</li><li> Go to the menu - Inventory</li><li> Select Crate and click “Open”</li></ol><hr><h2 id=\"extra\"> ? Useful links</h2><ul><li> <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/drops/campaigns\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Active Twitch Drops Campaigns</a></li><li> <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/drops/inventory\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">My inventory of drops</a></li></ul>'),
