(18330, 'en-US', 'Soap fix in RUST'),
(18331, 'en-US', 'How to Fix the Soapy Textures Issue in Rust...'),
(18332, 'en-US', '<h2>? Fix soap on textures in RUST</h2><h3> ? F1 - Console - Insert command</h3><p> ?Team:<br> <code>texture.memory_budget_factor 2</code></p><p> ?Select a server to play: <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/servers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">prostoj.store/servers</a></p><h3> ? Join our <a href=\"https://discord.gg/prostoj\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Discord community</a> and stay up to date!</h3>'),
(18333, 'en-US', 'Breaking: Rust August Update Bug - Tier 3 Workbench Not Working | Gaming News'),
(18334, 'en-US', 'After the update 08/08/2025 in Rust, the Tier 3 workbench broke - Tier 2 appears instead. The developers are aware of the problem and are preparing a fix.'),
(18335, 'en-US', '<h2>What happened?</h2><p> Since the release of the update on August 8, 2025, Rust players have been reporting a critical bug: <strong>the Tier 3 Workbench disappears</strong> , and a Tier 2 Workbench is displayed in the interface instead.</p><p> Because of this, it is impossible to craft on all servers, including official ones:</p><ul><li> Rockets and explosives</li><li> High-level weapons (LR-300, M249, etc.)</li><li> Other Tier 3 items</li></ul><h2> Developers\' reaction</h2><p> The Facepunch Studios team has already confirmed the issue on <a href=\"https://twitter.com/playrust\" rel=\"nofollow\">their official Twitter</a> and is working on a fix. The patch is expected to be released in the next 24-48 hours.</p><blockquote><p> \"We are aware of the bug with the Tier 3 workbench. A hotfix is in the works, stay tuned. Sorry for the inconvenience!\" - the lead developer said.</p></blockquote><h2> Temporary solution</h2><p> Until the issue is resolved, players recommend:</p><ol><li> Do not destroy existing Tier 3 workbenches</li><li> Postpone raids that require missiles</li><li> Use alternative weapons (eg from Tier 2)</li></ol><p> The update will be updated as information becomes available. Keep an eye on the official Rust channels.</p>'),
(18336, 'en-US', 'Triangular bed with enough space to plant 4 seeds.'),
(18337, 'en-US', 'Triangular Plantation'),
(18338, 'en-US', 'Pies'),
(18339, 'en-US', 'Small Oil Rig RUST | Guide'),
(18340, 'en-US', 'How to loot a small oil rig Rust...'),
(18341, 'en-US', '<header><h1>Small Oil Rig in Rust</h1> <a href=\"https://ibb.co/ynHT88FQ\"><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/hR35KKFm/image-16-1024x579-1.png\" alt=\"small oil rig rust\" border=\"0\"></a><p> <strong>The small oil rig</strong> is one of the rare objects <em>in Rust</em> that is of great interest to players. Here you can find resources, fight with guards and organize a good raid. In this article, we will figure out why this RT is needed, how to get there and what useful things can be obtained.</p></header><main><nav class=\"toc\" aria-label=\"Оглавление\"> <strong>Content</strong><ol><li> <a href=\"#about\">General description</a></li><li> <a href=\"#access\">Ways to get there</a></li><li> <a href=\"#respawn\">Update time</a></li><li> <a href=\"#looting\">Floor analysis</a><ol><li> <a href=\"#level-0\">Floor 0</a></li><li> <a href=\"#level-1\">Floor 1</a></li><li> <a href=\"#level-2\">Floor 2</a></li><li> <a href=\"#level-3\">Floor 3</a></li><li> <a href=\"#level-4\">Floor 4</a></li></ol></li><li> <a href=\"#cards\">Required access cards</a></li><li> <a href=\"#event\">Special event with military crate</a></li><li> <a href=\"#cameras\">CCTV cameras</a></li></ol></nav><section id=\"about\"><h2> General description</h2><p> <strong>The Small Oil Rig</strong> is a smaller version of the larger rig, located in the ocean near the shoreline. It has several levels, scattered with chests containing valuable loot. The facility also contains a boat for returning to land and a landing pad for aircraft.</p><p> <strong>The security</strong> is represented by armed scientists - there are more than ten of them, and it is quite difficult to deal with them alone.</p></section><section id=\"access\"><h2> Ways to get there</h2><p> Unlike land monuments, this location is isolated by water. There are two main ways to get there: by sea and by air.</p><h3> On the water</h3><p> It is best to use <strong>a boat with a motor</strong> or <strong>a rubber boat</strong> . Having swum to the platform, you can climb the stairs. If desired, the player can also swim, but this is risky.</p><h3> By air</h3><p> You can fly there by <strong>mini-copter</strong> , <strong>helicopter</strong> or <strong>hot air balloon</strong> . There is a separate landing site at the top. </p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/GQkvDdQW/Untitled-7-1-1-1024x576.png\" alt=\"landing on an oil rig\" border=\"0\"></section><section id=\"respawn\"><h2> Update time</h2><p> The speed of respawning boxes depends on the server configuration. In most cases, resources respawn in about <strong>half an hour</strong> .</p></section><section id=\"looting\"><h2> Floor analysis</h2><p> The platform is divided into several levels, each containing enemies and chests with loot. </p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/pBP7wCCk/Untitled-8-1-1-1024x527.png\" alt=\"oil rig floors\" border=\"0\"><article id=\"level-0\"><h3> Floor 0</h3><ul><li> Enemy: <strong>1 scientist</strong> .</li><li> Contents: a pair of boxes.</li><li> Transition: stairs in the center under the drilling rig.</li></ul></article><article id=\"level-1\"><h3> Floor 1</h3><ul><li> Loot: military, medical and regular crates, as well as fuel.</li><li> Enemies: <strong>2 scientists</strong> .</li><li> Further path: ladder under the crane or near the helicopter pad. </li></ul><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/GfY2WPgV/image.png\" alt=\"floor 1 of the oil rig\" border=\"0\"></article><article id=\"level-2\"><h3> Floor 2</h3><ul><li> Loot: up to <strong>10</strong> boxes of different types plus fuel.</li><li> Enemies: <strong>5 scientists</strong> .</li><li> The way up is either of the two stairs. </li></ul><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/WNSYKZXK/image.png\" alt=\"floor 2 of the oil rig\" border=\"0\"></article><article id=\"level-3\"><h3> Floor 3</h3><ul><li> Loot: about <strong>7</strong> boxes of varying rarity.</li><li> Enemies: <strong>2 scientists</strong> .</li><li> Features: There is <strong>a disposal unit</strong> , as well as <strong>a green door</strong> with military chests.</li><li> The way up: one of the stairs. </li></ul><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/WNSYKZXK/image.png\" alt=\"floor 3 of the oil rig\" border=\"0\"></article><article id=\"level-4\"><h3> Floor 4</h3><ul><li> Extraction: up to <strong>10</strong> boxes of different types plus fuel.</li><li> Enemies: <strong>6 scientists</strong> .</li><li> Features: <strong>Blue door</strong> with military grade loot and an additional room opened <strong>by a fuse</strong> . </li></ul><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/TM4n5s7V/image.png\" alt=\"floor 4 of the oil rig\" border=\"0\"></article></section><section id=\"cards\"><h2> Required access cards</h2><ul><li> <strong>Green Card</strong> - Opens a room on the third level with military loot.</li><li> <strong>Blue Card</strong> - Used on the fourth level, where boxes with valuable items are hidden.</li></ul></section><section id=\"event\"><h2> Special event with military crate</h2><p> At the very top is hidden <strong>a military crate</strong> . When activated, a mini-event begins:</p><ul><li> <strong>A siren</strong> is activated that can be heard by other players.</li><li> A helicopter arrives with <strong>5 reinforced scientists</strong> .</li><li> A timer starts for <strong>15 minutes</strong> , after which the box can be opened.</li></ul><p class=\"note\"> <strong>Objective:</strong> withstand enemy attacks and protect the point from competitors until the end of the timer to collect the reward.</p></section><section id=\"cameras\"><h2> CCTV cameras</h2><p> To connect to cameras on site, use the following codes:</p><ul><li> <code>OILRIG1L4</code></li><li> <code>OILRIG1L3</code></li><li> <code>OILRIG1L2</code></li><li> <code>OILRIG1L1</code></li><li> <code>OILRIG1DOCK</code></li><li> <code>OILRIG1HELI</code></li></ul></section></main><footer><p> © Rust Guide: Small Oil Rig.</p></footer>'),
(18342, 'en-US', 'Big Oil Rig RUST | Guide'),
(18343, 'en-US', 'How to loot a large oil rig Rust...'),
(18344, 'en-US', '<header><h1>Big oil rig in Rust</h1><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/XftqpLxg/image.png\" alt=\"image\" border=\"0\"><p> <strong>The Big Oil Rig</strong> is one of the most valuable and challenging <em>monuments</em> in <em>Rust</em> . It was introduced in the <strong>QoL</strong> Update (April 5, 2019) and has been a key target for experienced players ever since. In this guide, we will analyze what awaits you on the rig, what resources you can find and what dangers you will have to overcome.</p></header><main><nav class=\"toc\" aria-label=\"Оглавление\"> <strong>Content</strong><ol><li> <a href=\"#crates\">Where to look for boxes</a></li><li> <a href=\"#utilities\">Recycler, Workbench and Study Table</a></li><li> <a href=\"#rooms\">Closed rooms</a></li><li> <a href=\"#cameras\">Camera codes</a></li></ol></nav><section id=\"crates\"><h2> Where to look for boxes</h2><article id=\"dock\"><h3> Zero level (berth)</h3><p> There is no loot on the starting platform, but you will encounter <strong>two scientist guards</strong> who are covering the approach to the oil rig.</p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/278S0VgG/image.png\" alt=\"image\" border=\"0\"><article id=\"level-1\"><h3>First level</h3><p> There won\'t be any crates here either. <strong>Three scientists</strong> patrol the floor, preventing players from going higher without a fight.</p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/Xfs6f2s3/image.png\" alt=\"image\" border=\"0\"><article id=\"level-2\"><h3>Second level</h3><ul><li> Loot: regular, military and medical boxes.</li><li> Security: <strong>3 scientists</strong> . </li></ul><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/84G6vWHD/image.png\" alt=\"image\" border=\"0\"><article id=\"level-3\"><h3> Third level</h3><ul><li> Loot: 1-2 boxes + closed <strong>green room</strong> with valuable resources.</li><li> Security: <strong>4 scientists</strong> . </li></ul><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/Kpn0zNrG/image.png\" alt=\"image\" border=\"0\"><article id=\"level-4\"><h3> Fourth level</h3><ul><li> Loot: A couple of boxes in an open area + 2 closed rooms.</li><li> Security: <strong>3 scientists</strong> . </li></ul><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/yFmvXtPG/image.png\" alt=\"image\" border=\"0\"><article id=\"level-5\"><h3> Fifth level</h3><p> There is more open loot here, and the best boxes are hidden in <strong>the ventilation shafts</strong> . Elite boxes can be found.</p><p> Security: <strong>3 scientists</strong> .</p><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/yxHnRSL/image.png\" alt=\"image\" border=\"0\"><article id=\"level-6\"><h3> Sixth level (upper)</h3><p> There are crates on the roof and near <strong>the helipad</strong> , but most of the loot is hidden in a locked room. There is <strong>a locked military crate</strong> here that, when cracked, yields:</p><ul><li> the alarm goes off,</li><li> a helicopter arrives with <strong>11 elite scientists</strong> ,</li><li> The timer is turned on for 15 minutes.</li></ul><p> After the countdown is over, you can pick up the top loot. </p></article></article></article></article></article></article></article></section><section id=\"utilities\"><h2> Recycler, Workbench and Study Table</h2><ul><li> <strong>Workbench Level II</strong> - in the green room on the 3rd floor.</li><li> <strong>The Recycler</strong> is behind the door with the fuse on the 4th floor.</li><li> <strong>Study Table</strong> - Under the helipad on the upper level. </li></ul><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/LhD3stkc/image.png\" alt=\"image\" border=\"0\"><img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/2xFfZ9j/image.png\" alt=\"image\" border=\"0\"><section id=\"rooms\"><h2> Closed spaces</h2><p> There are rooms on the oil rig that can only be opened with access cards and fuses:</p><ul><li> <strong>3rd floor</strong> - green card (boxes + level II workbench).</li><li> <strong>4th floor</strong> - blue card (loot room) and fuse (recycler + blue card).</li><li> <strong>Floor 6</strong> - red card (top loot and war box).</li></ul></section><section id=\"cameras\"><h2> Camera codes</h2><p> The large oil rig is equipped with a video surveillance system. Below is a list of available codes:</p><ul><li> <code>OILRIG2L6D</code> , <code>OILRIG2L6C</code> , <code>OILRIG2L6B</code> , <code>OILRIG2L6A</code></li><li> <code>OILRIG2EXHAUST</code> , <code>OILRIG2HELI</code></li><li> <code>OILRIG2L5</code> , <code>OILRIG2L4</code></li><li> <code>OILRIG2L3B</code> , <code>OILRIG2L3A</code></li><li> <code>OILRIG2L2</code> , <code>OILRIG2L1</code> , <code>OILRIG2DOCK</code></li></ul></section></section></main><footer><p> © Rust Guide: Big Oil Rig.</p></footer>'),
(18345, 'en-US', 'Adding prohibited: the work is approved by the developers and is available in the store'),
(18346, 'en-US', 'Trade created'),
(18347, 'en-US', 'Secret map'),
(18348, 'en-US', 'Small Oil Rig RUST | Guide'),
(18349, 'en-US', '?DLC DECOR | And much more!'),
(18350, 'en-US', 'New DLC, sound improvements, ghost ships possible..'),
(18351, 'en-US', '<h1>? News from the world of Rust ?</h1><p> Fresh details on the updates: new lighting DLC, reworked weapon sound ranges and more!</p><h2> ? DLC \"Lighting Decor\"</h2><p> An add-on is coming soon that will expand the possibilities for base customization. The pack is filled with decorative and functional elements that will make your buildings more stylish and cozy. Here\'s what will be available: </p><h2><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/uploads/blog/20250828_204509_lsKtjBbv_photo_2025-08-28_21-44-59.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1086\" height=\"477\"></h2><p> Clothes mannequin - combines the functions of a cabinet and decoration, supports different poses.</p><ul><li> Garlands for creating atmospheric lighting.</li><li> Bean bag chairs (fabric and leather) for coziness.</li><li> Wall cabinet with lighting and through power supply.</li><li> Fluorescent lamps for soft lighting.</li><li> Electric table with integrated lamps.</li><li> Tripod and wall mounted floodlights for work areas.</li><li> Retro style pendant lamp. <h2><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/uploads/blog/20250828_204703_dtTdoTxW_photo_2025-08-28_21-46-11.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1096\" height=\"616\"></h2></li></ul><p></p><p> According to preliminary data, the update will be released next week. This is one of the most meaningful DLCs for those who love decorating bases. <em>A bit of irony: it seems that the developers were more carried away by releasing decorative sets than working on the main gameplay. Who knows, maybe one day we will see a paid DLC with a new color scheme for the sky or water ?</em></p><h2> ? Weapon sounds refinement</h2><p> The plan is to increase the range of gunshot audibility. Now:</p><ul><li> Any weapon will be distinguishable from about 400 m (previously it was about 350 m).</li><li> Powerful HMLMG, M249 machine guns and minigun - up to 600 m.</li><li> LR and AK rifles - about 500 m.</li><li> L96 and bolt-action rifle - up to 700 m.</li></ul><p> This way, players will be able to spot shootouts in advance or, conversely, avoid them.</p><h2> ? Deep Sea Zone</h2><p> The developers continue to work on a new ocean biome. Key points:</p><ul><li> Portals to enter the deep sea sector are added.</li><li> Around the perimeter there is radiation and a rougher sea.</li><li> There are hints of ghost ships and sunken islands with loot.</li></ul><p> This zone will be part of the upcoming <strong>Naval Update</strong> and is actively being worked on.</p><h2> ? Corrections</h2><ul><li> Fixed the operation of shelves on tugs.</li><li> Fixed display of favorite servers.</li><li> Fixed a bug with characters\' eyes closed.</li><li> Fixed zoomitem NRE crash.</li><li> The Discord button in the settings started working.</li><li> The number of stacks issued is limited (to prevent bugs).</li><li> Barricades can now be correctly placed near the railroad tracks near the RT.</li></ul><h2> ♻ Other changes</h2><ul><li> Working on a new test island for quality control.</li><li> Naval Update Development: AI for NPC ships, floating cities and other elements.</li><li> Optimization of leaf displacement.</li><li> Moved <em>vClouds</em> option to graphics settings.</li><li> New chainsaw animation.</li><li> Added a tooltip for the compass display function.</li><li> Team sleeping bag icons now only show if you have the build privilege and a hammer.</li></ul>'),
(18352, 'en-US', 'Name of the building'),
(18353, 'en-US', 'Skin name'),
(18354, 'en-US', 'Blog categories'),
(18355, 'en-US', 'Diesel in Rust: where to find and what it gives. Large quarry and sulfur quarry - numbers, radiation, launch'),
(18356, 'en-US', 'Where to get diesel in Rust (Sphere, Dump, oil rigs, Peaceful City), how many resources does 1 diesel give on a large excavator and on sulfur/stone/MVK quarries, what radiation and how to start. Extraction tables, short tips.');
INSERT INTO `language_translate` (`id`, `language`, `translation`) VALUES
(18357, 'en-US', '<h2>Content</h2><ul><li> <a href=\"#diesel\">What is diesel fuel</a></li><li> <a href=\"#where\">Where to find diesel</a></li><li> <a href=\"#excavator\">Large Quarry (Giant Excavator): Launch, Radiation, Extraction</a></li><li> <a href=\"#tables\">How many resources from 1 diesel: tables</a></li><li> <a href=\"#sulfur-quarry\">Sulfur quarry: how it works and how much it produces</a></li><li> <a href=\"#smart-home\">\"Smart Home\" at the Quarry: What Can Really Be Automated</a></li><li> <a href=\"#faq\">FAQ</a></li></ul><section id=\"diesel\"><h2> What is diesel fuel</h2><p> <strong>Diesel fuel</strong> is needed to operate <em>the Giant Excavator</em> , <em>quarries</em> (stone, sulfur, MWC) and <em>the pump tower (Pump Jack)</em> . It cannot be crafted or studied: canisters are mined at locations and bought in the Peaceful City. The maximum stack is <strong>20.</strong> One canister rotates the excavator for about <strong>2 minutes</strong> . In an hour, ≈ <strong>30</strong> canisters will be used.</p></section><section id=\"where\"><h2> Where to find diesel</h2><p> Reliable methods:</p><ul><li> <strong>Peaceful City (Outpost):</strong> Purchase for <strong>300</strong> <em>Low Quality Fuel</em> per canister.</li><li> <strong>Spawns on monuments:</strong> Sphere (2 points), Dump (≈2–3), Small and Large Oil Rigs (≈2 and ≈3). Also found on large \"radtown\" monuments. Respawn timers are short. </li></ul><!-- Изображения: замените src на свои файлы --><div><figure style=\"text-align: left; display: block;\"><img style=\"display: inline-block;\" src=\"/uploads/blog/20250829_010827_zTAa4opN_photo_2025-08-28_16-43-59.jpg\" alt=\"Sphere: places of diesel appearance\" width=\"525\" height=\"401\"><figcaption style=\"text-align: left;\"> Sphere: usually up to 2 canisters on the top tier. <br><br></figcaption></figure></div><div><figure style=\"text-align: left; display: block;\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250829_010952_NDzuBC9A_photo_2025-08-28_16-43-58.jpg\" alt=\"Peaceful City: Diesel Store\" width=\"309\" height=\"226\"><figcaption style=\"text-align: left;\"> Peaceful city: purchase of diesel for 300 TNK (Low Grade Fuel). <br><br></figcaption></figure></div><div><figure style=\"text-align: left; display: block;\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250829_011020_f7MHKSdC_photo_2025-08-28_16-43-59__2_.jpg\" alt=\"Dump: Diesel Spawn Points\" width=\"565\" height=\"428\"><figcaption style=\"text-align: left;\"> Dump: Several spawn points on the site and above the conveyor. <br><br></figcaption></figure></div><div><figure style=\"text-align: left; display: block;\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250829_011048_MSMlNGj-_photo_2025-08-28_16-43-59__3_.jpg\" alt=\"Small Oil Rig: Diesel Spawn\" width=\"577\" height=\"435\"><figcaption style=\"text-align: left;\"> Small oil rig: diesel is found on floors except the pier. <br><br></figcaption></figure></div><div><figure style=\"text-align: left; display: block;\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250829_011102_bTePHaJn_photo_2025-08-28_16-43-59__4_.jpg\" alt=\"Big Oil Rig: Diesel Spawn\" width=\"545\" height=\"396\"><figcaption style=\"text-align: left;\"> Large oil rig: usually found on the upper levels.<br><br></figcaption></figure></div></section><section id=\"excavator\"><h2> Large Quarry (Giant Excavator): Launch, Radiation, Extraction</h2><h3> How to launch</h3><ol><li> Clear out the scientists on the monument grounds.</li><li> Go up to the engine room, insert the diesel into the fuel tank.</li><li> Turn on the engine and select the resource type on the control panel.</li><li> Collect resources from two drop points on either side of the boom.</li></ol><h3> Radiation</h3><p> Radiation is low throughout the area. For most points, <strong>~11% protection</strong> is enough (a burlap set will do), but hazmat is more reliable, especially closer to the engine.</p></section><section id=\"tables\"><h2> How many resources from 1 diesel: tables</h2><h3> Giant excavator</h3><table><thead><tr><th> Mode</th><th> Output from 1 diesel</th><th> Time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Stone</td><td> 10,000 stones</td><td> ~2 min</td></tr><tr><td> Metal</td><td> 5,000 metal fragments</td><td> ~2 min</td></tr><tr><td> Sulfur</td><td> 2,000 sulfur ore</td><td> ~2 min</td></tr><tr><td> MVC</td><td> 100 high quality ore</td><td> ~2 min</td></tr></tbody></table><p> The numbers correspond to the official production buff of the excavator.</p><h3> Quarries on the map (stone, sulfur, MVK)</h3><table><thead><tr><th> Quarry type</th><th> Output from 1 diesel</th><th> Time</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Stone quarry</td><td> 5000 stone + 1000 metal ore</td><td> ~2 min 10 sec</td></tr><tr><td> Sulfur quarry</td><td> 1,000 sulfur ore</td><td> ~2 min 10 sec</td></tr><tr><td> MVK quarry</td><td> 50 MVK ore</td><td> ~2 min 10 sec</td></tr></tbody></table><p> Stats for public monument careers; may vary on mod servers.</p></section><section id=\"sulfur-quarry\"><h2> Sulfur quarry: how it works and how much it produces</h2><p> The Sulfur Quarry is a monument with a permanent extraction point. The player brings a diesel, starts the installation and gets a stable <strong>~1,000 sulfur ore for 1 diesel</strong> in ~2 minutes. At the start of the raid, this is enough for gunpowder and C4, and in a \"long\" game it is more profitable to alternate extraction on the excavator (2,000/diesel) and at the quarry itself, so as not to be seen by the entire server.</p><h3> Short instruction</h3><ul><li> Bring the required number of canisters.</li><li> Insert diesel into the tank and activate.</li><li> Defend the point: the noise is low, but players often check the monument.</li></ul></section><section id=\"smart-home\"><h2> \"Smart Home\" at the Quarry: What Can Really Be Automated</h2><p> Quarries and the excavator do not have their own power ports. Automation concerns <em>your base</em> nearby: power from solar panels and batteries, motion sensors, sirens, turrets, smart switches and Rust+ notifications on the phone. This helps to hold the point while the quarry is working. Practice a separate loot room and a bunker door on the exit to the monument.</p></section><section id=\"faq\"><h2> FAQ</h2><p> <strong>How many resources does 1 diesel engine provide on an excavator?</strong><br> Stone - 10k, metal - 5k fragments, sulfur - 2k ore, MWK - 100. ~2 minutes per canister.</p><p> <strong>How much does a large quarry produce per hour?</strong><br> Approximately 30 canisters will burn in an hour (2 minutes per canister). Multiply the numbers from the table by 30.</p><p> <strong>How much radiation is there in a large quarry?</strong><br> Low. Aim for about 11% protection; hazmat covers the entire area.</p><p> <strong>Where is the fastest place to assemble a diesel engine?</strong><br> Purchase at Outpost for 300 TNK and quick runs through the Sphere, Dump and oil rigs.</p></section><p> <strong>Important:</strong> the numbers are valid for vanilla servers. On mod projects, admins often change the rates of production and spawn. Check the server rules.</p>'),
(18358, 'en-US', 'Rust - Common Errors and Quick Fixes (EAC, Steam Auth Timeout, Crashes, Microphone, Servers)'),
(18359, 'en-US', 'List of common Rust errors and simple steps: EAC Authentication Timeout, Steam Auth Timeout, Unknown file version, Untrusted system file, missing servers, crashes during Asset Warmup, microphone problems. Table of quick solutions and short instructions.'),
(18360, 'en-US', '<h2>Content</h2><ul><li> <a href=\"#quick\">Quick solutions</a></li><li> <a href=\"#eac\">EAC Authentication Timeout / EAC Disconnected</a></li><li> <a href=\"#steam-auth\">Disconnected: Steam Auth Timeout</a></li><li> <a href=\"#unknown-file\">Unknown file version / Integrity error</a></li><li> <a href=\"#untrusted\">Untrusted system file</a></li><li> <a href=\"#vcruntime\">Doesn\'t start: VCRUNTIME/MSVCP</a></li><li> <a href=\"#servers\">Servers are not displayed</a></li><li> <a href=\"#asset-warmup\">Crash/freeze during Asset Warmup</a></li><li> <a href=\"#mic\">The microphone does not work</a></li><li> <a href=\"#version\">Incompatible version / Server is newer</a></li><li> <a href=\"#ban\">EAC/VAC ban</a></li><li> <a href=\"#faq\">FAQ</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"quick\"> Quick solutions</h2><table><thead><tr><th> Symptom</th><th> What to do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> EAC Authentication Timeout / EAC Disconnected</td><td> Launch from Steam, check files, run Repair in Easy Anti-Cheat, reboot PC and router.</td></tr><tr><td> Disconnected: Steam Auth Timeout</td><td> Restart Steam and the game, clear the Steam download cache, check files, check server status.</td></tr><tr><td> Unknown file version / Integrity error</td><td> Delete the specified file and check its integrity, disable software that changes game files.</td></tr><tr><td> Untrusted system file</td><td> Run <code>sfc /scannow</code> , install Windows updates, Repair EAC again.</td></tr><tr><td> VCRUNTIME/ MSVCP missing</td><td> Install Microsoft Visual C++ 2015–2022 (x64 and x86), restart your PC.</td></tr><tr><td> The server is not displayed in the list</td><td> Raise the ping limit in Steam, update the game/server, connect via F1: <code>client.connect IP:port</code> .</td></tr><tr><td> Asset Warmup crash/freeze</td><td> Check files, update video card driver, increase swap file, close overlays.</td></tr><tr><td> The microphone does not work</td><td> Select an input device in Windows/Steam/Rust, disable unnecessary microphones and overlays.</td></tr><tr><td> Incompatible version</td><td> Update the client. The server may be newer on the day of the wipe.</td></tr><tr><td> EAC/VAC ban</td><td> The ban is permanent. Appeals are via EAC; dev-bans for behavior are not removed.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id=\"eac\"> EAC Authentication Timeout / EAC Disconnected</h2><ol><li> Launch Rust from your Steam library, not from the game folder.</li><li> Steam → Rust Properties → Installed Files → \"Verify Integrity of Files\".</li><li> Open the game folder and run <code>EasyAntiCheat_EOS_Setup.exe</code> → «Repair Service».</li><li> Restart your PC and router. Temporarily disable VPN/overlays.</li><li> Check if the server is being updated. </li></ol><figure><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250829_021513_m1MkzlBp_steam-open-game-properties.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"623\" height=\"502\"><figcaption></figcaption></figure><figure style=\"text-align: left;\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250829_021524_nSVz6IUh_steam_verify_2.jpg\" alt=\"Repair Easy Anti-Cheat for Rust\" width=\"616\" height=\"600\"><figcaption style=\"text-align: left;\"> Repair in Easy Anti-Cheat.</figcaption></figure><h2 id=\"steam-auth\"> Disconnected: Steam Auth Timeout</h2><p> This is a Steamworks authentication timeout. Usually the network or Steam itself is to blame.</p><ol><li> Restart Steam and Rust.</li><li> Steam → Settings → Downloads → “Clear download cache” (requires re-authorization).</li><li> Check the integrity of the files.</li><li> If the server is being updated or is unavailable, try again later or go to another one.</li></ol><h2 id=\"unknown-file\"> Unknown file version / Integrity error</h2><p> Usually one of the game files is damaged or modified.</p><ol><li> Look at the file path in the error message, delete it.</li><li> Check the integrity in Steam - the client will finish downloading the original.</li><li> Disable software that interferes with files: mod utilities, overlays, \"optimizers\".</li></ol><h2 id=\"untrusted\"> Untrusted system file</h2><p> A system library has been loaded that does not pass verification.</p><ol><li> Command line from administrator: <code>sfc /scannow</code> .</li><li> Install the latest Windows updates.</li><li> Repeat Repair in Easy Anti-Cheat.</li></ol><h2 id=\"vcruntime\"> Rust won\'t start: \"VCRUNTIME140.dll/MSVCP140.dll is missing\"</h2><p> Install Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable 2015–2022 for x64 and x86. Restart your PC after installation.</p><h2 id=\"servers\"> Servers are not displayed in the list</h2><ol><li> Steam → Settings → “In game” → “Server browser pings per minute” ≥ 5000.</li><li> Update the client and the server itself to the same version.</li><li> Connect directly: F1 → <code>client.connect IP:port</code> .</li></ol><h2 id=\"asset-warmup\"> Crash/freeze during Asset Warmup or when entering the server</h2><ol><li> Verifying files in Steam.</li><li> Update your graphics card driver (NVIDIA/AMD/Intel).</li><li> Increase the Windows paging file (virtual memory).</li><li> Close background programs and overlays.</li></ol><h2 id=\"mic\"> The microphone does not work</h2><ol><li> Windows: Select the desired default microphone and disable unnecessary devices.</li><li> Steam: \"Voice\" → correct input and microphone test.</li><li> Rust: Check the input device and Push-to-Talk button.</li></ol><h2 id=\"version\"> \"Incompatible version\" / \"Server is running a newer version\"</h2><p> Update the client. On the day of the forced wipe, the official server may be temporarily newer.</p><h2 id=\"ban\"> EAC/VAC ban</h2><p> The ban is permanent. Erroneous waves are rolled back automatically. Appeals are submitted to EAC. Devbans for toxicity are not removed. </p><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250829_021549_9aGMShtP_mceu_20981317611756422947896.jpg\" width=\"484\" height=\"272\"></p><h2 id=\"faq\"> FAQ</h2><p> <strong>Where to start if “nothing helps”?</strong><br> Check files, Repair EAC, reboot PC and router. This closes most cases.</p><p> <strong>Is it possible to play with VPN enabled?</strong><br> Better to disable. Some VPNs break authorization and connection to Steam.</p><p> <strong>Why can\'t the server be found via search, but the IP connection works?</strong><br> Server browser restrictions and filters. Use direct connection.</p><p> <strong>Important:</strong> Error wording and behavior may differ on mod servers. Follow the basic steps first, then check the rules and versions on a specific project.</p>'),
