(18521, 'en-US', '<h1>Wipe on X2 and MAX4X2</h1><ul><li> ? Don\'t forget to vote for the map on the server:</li><li> <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/maps/classicx2\">⚡X2 [weekly]</a></li><li> <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/maps/max4x2\">⚡MAX4 X2</a></li><li> ? WIPE 12.09 at 16:00 MSK! (change of map)</li><li> ? Only players who have played on the server for more than 1 hour can vote for the map.</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th> Server</th><th> Rates</th><th> Connection</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> SIMPLE #2 [X2-week]</td><td> X2, weekly, skin giveaway</td><td> <code>connect 185.189.255.160:35000</code></td></tr><tr><td> SIMPLE #7 [MAX4 X2]</td><td> X2, weekly, limit 4 people</td><td> <code>connect 195.18.27.175:35200</code></td></tr></tbody></table><h1> And there\'s a new update coming to Rust!</h1><ul><li> You can put grenades, bee grenades, C4 and more into drones on the stage branch. <br><br><video style=\"width: 900px; height: 450px;\" controls=\"controls\" width=\"778\" height=\"389\"><source src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/783409583162261595/1415064728979378326/Rust_New_Drone_Meta_Drop_Grenade_Bees_C4_Satchels_get-save.com.mp4?ex=68c281fa&amp;is=68c1307a&amp;hm=bc7805efd2e7a682c57739fbe0988c5da8d0165122d74619d60ff2c3fa30ed83&amp;\"></video><br><br></li></ul>'),
(18522, 'en-US', 'Guide on how to loot a Rocket Silo | Rust, Guide, Rocket'),
(18523, 'en-US', 'Guide to looting a missile launch silo.'),
(18524, 'en-US', '<h1>Missile silo</h1><p> In this guide, we will take a detailed look at the Missile Silo monument: where to look, what to take with you, what threats to expect, and how to effectively complete the location to get the maximum amount of loot. <br><br><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/silo_main.webp\" alt=\"silo_main\" width=\"866\" height=\"487\"></p><h2> Briefly about the monument</h2><p> The Missile Silo is one of the most coveted monuments in Rust: it has a large amount of useful loot, but also a lot of risk. The main dangers are scientists (many with NVG and high damage), dangerous falls into the silo, a hot or dangerous hatch, and of course hostile players who can ambush you at the exit or hide inside.</p><h2> Enemies and loot</h2><ul><li> Bots: 27 in total - 4 of which are regular patrol scientists and 23 with NVG.</li><li> Loot: Around 30 regular/military crates, 1 elite crate, 3 diesel barrels and a red card at the bottom.</li></ul><h2> What to take with you</h2><ul><li> Blue card - required to open the hatch.</li><li> Clothing with radiation protection ≥ 25. Hazmat will do, but a set with greater stability and survivability is preferable.</li><li> Weapons according to taste and skills.</li><li> Ammunition: If you are using an assault rifle (AK), aim for ~100 rounds.</li><li> Medicines and dressings.</li></ul><h2> Where is it located?</h2><p> Open the map - the mine usually lies on the border of the forest and desert biomes; it is visible as a large significant monument.<br><br><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250915_195242_Zl3K8IMB_mceclip0.png\" width=\"833\" height=\"525\"></p><h2>External structure and environment</h2><p> The mine area is located on a small hill and is fenced with barbed wire. There are three observation towers along the perimeter. In the center is a large hatch, surrounded by several utility buildings and hangars; barricades are scattered everywhere, which will come in handy in a shootout. A radio tower with a ladder is visible at the corner of the site.<br><br><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250915_195627_3TrpFo-q_mceclip1.png\" width=\"850\" height=\"503\"></p><h2>Internal structure (underground)</h2><p> Hidden beneath the surface is a multi-level complex with a network of corridors and rooms. There are 6 levels in height: from 0 to -5. Inside there are living quarters, offices, warehouses, bathrooms and elevators.<br><br><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250915_195707_QLsCotIw_mceclip2.png\" width=\"953\" height=\"474\"></p><h2>Detailed route of the cleanup</h2><h3> External part - order of bypass</h3><ol><li> House 1 (entrance near the barbed wire) - 1 box.</li><li> Near house 2 - 2 boxes near the house (you can\'t go inside).</li><li> House 3 - 2 boxes inside; when leaving, go to the hangars.</li><li> Hangars - shelves to the left (1 box) and right (3 boxes) of the truck.</li><li> House 5 - 1 box and a place to activate the blue card (20 seconds to jump into the hatch).<br><br></li></ol><p><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/schema.avif\" width=\"903\" height=\"508\"></p><h3>Underground part - sequence by levels</h3><h4> Level 0</h4><p> First flight, side room with a box, then stairs to -1. <br><br><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/level_0.avif\" alt=\"level_0\" width=\"473\" height=\"266\"><br><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/level1_stairs.avif\" alt=\"level1_stairs\" width=\"473\" height=\"266\"></p><h4> Level -1</h4><p> Crates near boxes and shelves; two rooms with green doors that may contain loot. Next is an elevator to -2.<br><br><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/level1.avif\" alt=\"level1\" width=\"475\" height=\"267\"><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/level1_1.avif\" alt=\"level1_1\" width=\"474\" height=\"267\"><br><br></p><h4> Level -2</h4><p> Two boxes by the elevator, then jump along the platforms into the shaft to -5.<br><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/level2_1.avif\" alt=\"level2_1\" width=\"476\" height=\"268\"></p><h4><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/level2_2.avif\" alt=\"level2_2\" width=\"478\" height=\"269\"><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/level2_3.avif\" alt=\"level2_3\" width=\"478\" height=\"269\"></h4><h4> Level -5 (heart of the mine)</h4><p> Bunker with warhead, laptop with timer, red card, elite box and 3 barrels of diesel. </p><p><br><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/level5_1.avif\" alt=\"level5_1\" width=\"480\" height=\"270\"></p><h4> Level -4</h4><p> A small computer room with one drawer. <br><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/computer_room.avif\" alt=\"computer_room\" width=\"480\" height=\"270\"></p><h4> Level -3</h4><p> Two living rooms: 2 boxes in the first, 1 in the second. Another one near the stairs. </p><p><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/living_quarters1.avif\" alt=\"living_quarters1\" width=\"485\" height=\"273\"></p><p><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/living_quarters2.avif\" alt=\"living_quarters2\" width=\"485\" height=\"273\"></p><h4> Second pass level -2 (exit block)</h4><p> Warehouses and toilets - extra boxes. The admin office is empty of loot, but behind it is a rack with two boxes. </p><p><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/stairs%20level2.avif\" alt=\"stairs level 2\" width=\"489\" height=\"275\"></p><h3> Exit</h3><p> We go up to -1, kill the last bots, go to the room with the camera computer and the red button. The door opens the exit outside. <br><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/silo_out_stairs.avif\" alt=\"silo_out_stairs\" width=\"491\" height=\"276\"><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/room_out.avif\" alt=\"room_out\" width=\"490\" height=\"276\"></p><h2> Tips and Warnings</h2><ul><li> Be careful around the hatch - its edges cause damage.</li><li> NVG bots are especially dangerous in dark places - use cover.</li><li> If you are on a team, assign roles.</li><li> The red card is needed for other monuments.</li><li> Look at the laptop near the warhead - there are event timers there. <br><br><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250915_201140_IoLeTAW7_mceclip3.png\" width=\"532\" height=\"219\"><img src=\"https://rustexplore.com/images/camera_silo.avif\" alt=\"camera_silo\" width=\"390\" height=\"219\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250915_201220_E1jDuXAi_mceclip4.png\" width=\"395\" height=\"219\"></li></ul><h2> Conclusion</h2><p> The Rocket Silo is a great place to get valuable items, but only with proper preparation and careful cleaning. Following the route and having everything you need, you can take out the maximum amount of resources.</p>'),
(18525, 'en-US', 'Guide | How to loot military tunnels in Rust | Tunnels, guide, rust'),
(18526, 'en-US', 'How to easily loot military tunnels in Rust..'),
(18527, 'en-US', '<article><h1>Military Tunnels Guide in Rust <br><img src=\"http://rustcraft.ru/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Screenshot_5-1024x637.png\" alt=\"RT \"Military Tunnels\" in Rust\" width=\"866\" height=\"539\"></h1><p> <strong>Military Tunnels</strong> are one of the most profitable locations for farming: a lot of loot, weak audibility of gunshots from the outside and a rich atmosphere. But the enemies here are serious, so it is important to be prepared. </p><p><img src=\"http://rustcraft.ru/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Military-tunnel-%D0%BD%D0%B0-%D0%B2%D0%BD%D1%83%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B8%D0%B3%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%BE%D0%B9-%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%82%D0%B5-%D0%B2-Rust.png\" alt=\"Military tunnel on the in-game map in Rust\"></p><h2> General information</h2><table><tbody><tr><th> Location</th><td> Underground complex</td></tr><tr><th> On the surface</th><td> Missile silo, destroyed tower, 2 mining tunnels</td></tr><tr><th> Entrance</th><td> Through the rails and the pile of cars</td></tr></tbody></table><h2> Radiation</h2><table><tbody><tr><th> Background</th><td> 10–25 units</td></tr><tr><th> Minimum protection</th><td> Pants + Sweatshirt + Boots + Wooden Armor</td></tr><tr><th> Optimal protection</th><td> Hazmat suit (can be obtained from scientists) </td></tr></tbody></table><h2><img src=\"https://images.steamusercontent.com/ugc/2537298107808829227/759EA664677405EFB76DCFA018A3E09E24AE83AA/\" alt=\"Steam Community :: Guide :: All Skins for Anti-Radiation Suit - Hazmat [UPD!]\" width=\"377\" height=\"377\"><br> Enemies</h2><table><tbody><tr><th> Quantity</th><td> 29 scientists</td></tr><tr><th> Weapon</th><td> M92, MP5A4, M39, LR-300</td></tr><tr><th> Peculiarities</th><td> Stronger than regular street bots </td></tr></tbody></table><h2><img src=\"https://cdn.rusthelp.com/images/256/hazmatsuit-scientist.webp\" alt=\"Scientist Costume | Rust Wiki\" width=\"376\" height=\"376\"><br> Access cards</h2><table><tbody><tr><th> Necessary cards</th><td> Green, blue, red</td></tr><tr><th> Additionally</th><td> Fuse</td></tr><tr><th> No cards</th><td> Access to open loot only (less profitable) </td></tr></tbody></table><h2><img src=\"https://moscow77.store/uploads/drop/951_1_603aa2d13ff6971b9b7c95c4bfab35fe.png\" alt=\"Access cards\" width=\"556\" height=\"556\"><br> Recycler</h2><table><tbody><tr><th> Location</th><td> A metal shed at the entrance to the second mining tunnel</td></tr><tr><th> Sign</th><td> It stands in a prominent place, hard to miss </td></tr></tbody></table><h2><img src=\"http://rustcraft.ru/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Screenshot_25-1.png\" alt=\"Shed with a recycler on the outskirts of the RT \"Military Tunnels\" in Rust\" width=\"620\" height=\"526\"><br> Farming step by step</h2><table><tbody><tr><th> Step</th><th> Action</th></tr><tr><td> 1</td><td> Collect barrels and boxes on the surface</td></tr><tr><td> 2</td><td> Clear the entrance of scientists</td></tr><tr><td> 3</td><td> Go inside with a weapon and a flashlight</td></tr><tr><td> 4</td><td> Inspect the arsenal on the right (several boxes, guarded by a scientist)</td></tr><tr><td> 5</td><td> Go along the left corridor (many bots, elite container at \"3\" on the wall)</td></tr><tr><td> 6</td><td> Solve the puzzle to access the main loot</td></tr></tbody></table><h2> Solving the puzzle</h2><table><tbody><tr><th> Action</th><th> Description</th></tr><tr><td> 1</td><td> Insert the fuse into the arsenal and activate the timer</td></tr><tr><td> 2</td><td> Run along the left path → crawl through the fence → climb up the stairs</td></tr><tr><td> 3</td><td> Open the green door <em>Storage</em> , clear the room</td></tr><tr><td> 4</td><td> Turn on the switch to power the lab</td></tr><tr><td> 5</td><td> Open the blue door <em>Laboratory</em></td></tr><tr><td> 6</td><td> Activate the timer and open the red door</td></tr><tr><td> 7</td><td> Deal with the guards (it\'s easier to use grenades)</td></tr></tbody></table><p> <strong><img src=\"http://rustcraft.ru/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Screenshot_20.png\" alt=\"Fuse holder and timer in the armory room at the Military Tunnels RT in Rust\" width=\"613\" height=\"543\"><br> Reward:</strong> 3 elite boxes, 2 military and 2 regular.</p><h2> Mining tunnels</h2><table><tbody><tr><th> Tunnel</th><th> Peculiarities</th></tr><tr><td> Small</td><td> Almost empty, just stone</td></tr><tr><td> Big</td><td> Barrels with components, military boxes, dark (need a flashlight) </td></tr></tbody></table><h2><img src=\"http://rustcraft.ru/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Screenshot_24-1.png\" alt=\"Entrance to the second mining tunnel at the Military Tunnels RT in Rust\" width=\"571\" height=\"409\"><br><img src=\"https://1lag.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/image-162-1024x576.jpeg\" width=\"572\" height=\"322\"><br> Cameras</h2><table><tbody><tr><th> Availability</th><td> There are no connected cameras in the location.</td></tr><tr><th> Extraction</th><td> Cameras can be found in elite boxes</td></tr><tr><th> Usage</th><td> Set up at base for surveillance via station </td></tr></tbody></table><br><img src=\"https://rustgame.ru/upload/img/_rust-camera.jpg\" alt=\"Passwords for all cameras in Rust | Rustgame\" width=\"495\" height=\"273\"></article>'),
(18528, 'en-US', 'Rust October 2025 Update: Blueprints, C4 Drones, Volcano and New Mechanics'),
(18529, 'en-US', 'The October Rust 2025 update brings back blueprint fragments for workbenches, drones gain the ability to carry explosives, a lava volcano appears, and barricades and monuments are reworked.');
INSERT INTO `language_translate` (`id`, `language`, `translation`) VALUES
(18530, 'en-US', '<h2>The return of the blueprint system</h2><p> Rust has reintroduced the blueprint fragment mechanic. Now, to craft workbenches, you will need to collect special items:</p><table><thead><tr><th> Workbench</th><th> Requirements</th><th> Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Tier 2</td><td> 5 regular fragments</td><td> There is no information about the drop yet</td></tr><tr><td> Tier 3</td><td> 5 advanced fragments</td><td> Crates (guaranteed), elite boxes (with a chance) </td></tr></tbody></table><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_143638_WyzPGZCi_BB685B35-356E-4BF7-A2EC-92F177BE1A82.png\" alt=\"Blueprint fragments in Rust\" width=\"608\" height=\"160\"></p><h2> Drones with explosives are the new meta</h2><p> On the staging branch, the developers are testing the ability to load explosive devices into drones. Now they can carry:</p><ul><li> regular grenades,</li><li> bee pomegranates,</li><li> C4,</li><li> and other items.</li></ul><p> In effect, drones are being turned into guided bombs. Tests have shown that the drone is capable of dropping smoke grenades, airdrops, individual weapons, and backpacks. Some objects, such as propane bombs or rockets, are not yet supported. </p><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_143653_vrfiEHgm_photo_2025-09-16_15-35-33.jpg\" alt=\"Rust Explosive Drones\" width=\"714\" height=\"332\"></p><h2> Changes on monuments</h2><ul><li> Diesel engine spawning has been changed at the Airfield and Wastewater Treatment Plants. It is now only given out after completing the map puzzle.</li><li> The Satellite Dishes and Dump have had their construction no-go zones made spherical, expanding the possibilities for nearby bases.</li><li> If the monument is in T1 or T2, the loot will be better than in T0.</li><li> Small Oil Rig no longer spawns in T0. </li></ul><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_143952_PHeTVECm_mceu_51874844211758022791013.png\" width=\"501\" height=\"426\"></p><h2> Balance of items</h2><p> Some items have received changes to their characteristics:</p><table><thead><tr><th> Item</th><th> Was</th><th> It became</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Wooden barricades (stack)</td><td> 5</td><td> 3</td></tr><tr><td> Wooden Barricades (HP)</td><td> 120</td><td> 80 </td></tr></tbody></table><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_143734_qMaYxKF8_sjFsj2V1s9SFn4kATPJISDafHmZTfjGpmwabbEFLw6DOCWpzVdIe6Fe4J_xAdg-PiM9ji6r5.png\" alt=\"Changes to wooden barricades\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\"></p><h2> New trap</h2><p> A new type of spike trap is in development. There is no exact information about its visuals and mechanics yet, but it is assumed that it will be placed in the ground.</p><h2> New monument - volcano</h2><p> Rust has a new development branch - Volcano. Work is underway on the model and lava, which will deal strong damage when touched and leave a burning effect. </p><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_143755_NYSmmnwn_44D3F3F7-A807-4705-9A7F-33AE610AF018.png\" alt=\"New Vulcan Monument in Rust\" width=\"544\" height=\"308\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_143841_rjy93yNf_photo_2025-09-16_15-38-27.jpg\" alt=\"Screenshot from the stage of the volcano branch\" width=\"573\" height=\"310\"></p><h2> Transport and mechanics</h2><p> The updated bike now has the ability to perform a bunny hop. To do this, you need to press the right mouse button, provided that the bike has stamina and is not flooded. You can use the trick once every three seconds. </p><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_144100_Z_irdWYI_mceu_89827215721758022859989.jpg\" width=\"586\" height=\"281\"></p><h2> Performance and upcoming plans</h2><p> After the latest patch, players noticed a drop in FPS. The developers confirmed the problems and promise optimizations this month. In addition, insiders reported that the marine update will be released in November.</p><h2> Results</h2><p> Rust is going through one of its biggest changes in a long time. The return of the blueprint system, drones with combat potential, new monuments, and item balancing could completely change the game\'s meta. Players will have to wait for the updates to hit the main client.</p><p> Try new mechanics on our servers on October 2: <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/servers\">https://prostoj.store/servers</a> .</p>'),
(18531, 'en-US', '<h2>Content</h2><ul><li> <a href=\"#blueprints\">Return of the blueprint system</a></li><li> <a href=\"#drones\">Explosive drones are the new meta.</a></li><li> <a href=\"#monuments\">Changes to monuments</a></li><li> <a href=\"#balance\">Item balance</a></li><li> <a href=\"#trap\">New trap</a></li><li> <a href=\"#volcano\">New monument - volcano</a></li><li> <a href=\"#transport\">Transport and mechanics</a></li><li> <a href=\"#missions\">New mission rewards</a></li><li> <a href=\"#rtupdate\">RT Update – Sphere Recycler and New Puzzles</a></li><li> <a href=\"#performance\">Performance and future plans</a></li><li> <a href=\"#summary\">Results</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"blueprints\"> Return of the blueprint system</h2><p> Rust has reintroduced the blueprint fragment mechanic. Now, crafting workbenches requires collecting special items:</p><table><thead><tr><th> Workbench</th><th> Requirements</th><th> Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Tier 2</td><td> 5 regular fragments</td><td> There is no information about the drop yet.</td></tr><tr><td> Tier 3</td><td> 5 advanced fragments</td><td> Crates (guaranteed), elite boxes (with a chance) </td></tr></tbody></table><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_143638_WyzPGZCi_BB685B35-356E-4BF7-A2EC-92F177BE1A82.png\" alt=\"Blueprint fragments in Rust\" width=\"608\" height=\"160\"></p><h2 id=\"drones\"> Explosive drones are the new meta.</h2><p> On the staging branch, the developers are testing the ability to load explosive devices onto drones. They can now carry:</p><ul><li> regular grenades,</li><li> bee pomegranates,</li><li> C4,</li><li> and other items.</li></ul><p> Drones are effectively being transformed into guided bombs. Tests have shown that the drone is capable of dropping smoke grenades, airdrops, individual weapons, and even backpacks. Some objects, such as propane bombs or rockets, are not yet supported. </p><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_143653_vrfiEHgm_photo_2025-09-16_15-35-33.jpg\" alt=\"Rust Explosive Drones\" width=\"714\" height=\"332\"></p><h2 id=\"monuments\"> Changes to monuments</h2><ul><li> The Diesel engine\'s appearance at the Airfield and Wastewater Treatment Plant has been changed. It is now only awarded after completing the map puzzle.</li><li> The Satellite Dishes and Dump have had their construction no-go zones made spherical, expanding the possibilities for nearby bases.</li><li> If the monument is in zone T1 or T2, the loot in it will be better than in zone T0.</li><li> The small oil platform no longer spawns in area T0. </li></ul><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_143952_PHeTVECm_mceu_51874844211758022791013.png\" width=\"501\" height=\"426\"></p><h2 id=\"balance\"> Item balance</h2><p> Some items have received changes to their characteristics:</p><table><thead><tr><th> Item</th><th> Was</th><th> It became</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Wooden barricades (stack)</td><td> 5</td><td> 3</td></tr><tr><td> Wooden Barricades (HP)</td><td> 120</td><td> 80 </td></tr></tbody></table><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_143734_qMaYxKF8_sjFsj2V1s9SFn4kATPJISDafHmZTfjGpmwabbEFLw6DOCWpzVdIe6Fe4J_xAdg-PiM9ji6r5.png\" alt=\"Changes to wooden barricades\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\"></p><h2 id=\"trap\"> New trap</h2><p> A new type of spike trap is in development. There\'s no precise information yet about its visuals or mechanics, but it\'s expected to be placed in the ground.</p><h2 id=\"volcano\"> New monument - volcano</h2><p> Rust has a new development branch: Volcano. Work is underway on the model and lava, which will deal significant damage on contact and leave a burning effect. </p><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_143755_NYSmmnwn_44D3F3F7-A807-4705-9A7F-33AE610AF018.png\" alt=\"New Vulcan monument in Rust\" width=\"544\" height=\"308\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_143841_rjy93yNf_photo_2025-09-16_15-38-27.jpg\" alt=\"Screenshot from the Volcano branch stage\" width=\"573\" height=\"310\"></p><h2 id=\"transport\"> Transport and mechanics</h2><p> The updated bike now has the ability to perform a bunny hop. To do this, press the right mouse button, provided the bike has stamina and isn\'t flooded. This trick can be performed once every three seconds. </p><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250916_144100_Z_irdWYI_mceu_89827215721758022859989.jpg\" width=\"586\" height=\"281\"></p><h2 id=\"missions\"> New mission rewards</h2><p> Rust\'s developers delighted players with a mission update—now you can earn more scrap, useful teas, and additional items for completing quests. Let\'s compare what\'s changed:</p><h3> ? Boar Hunter</h3><ul><li> Old reward: 100 scrap</li><li> New reward: Simple Ore Tea and 150 Scrap</li></ul><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250922_230846_uFNu8sP5_mceu_77669370641758571725954.jpg\"></p><h3> ? Deer Hunter</h3><ul><li> Old reward: 100 scrap</li><li> New reward: Simple Scrap Tea and 150 Scrap</li></ul><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250922_230816_ll60EMdq_mceu_47374116521758571695082.jpg\"></p><h3> ? Mission Fisherman</h3><ul><li> Old Award: Kayak and Paddle</li><li> New reward: Kayak, paddle, and 75 scrap</li></ul><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250922_230829_RZPJ_biE_mceu_35529043031758571708094.jpg\"></p><h3> ? Mission \"8 Barrels of Fuel\"</h3><ul><li> Old reward: 100 scrap</li><li> New reward: 250 scrap and 3 fish pies</li></ul><h3> ? Shark Hunting</h3><ul><li> Old reward: Drill, 3 syringes and 25 scrap</li><li> New reward: Drill, 3 syringes and 50 scrap</li></ul><h3> ? Mission Diving</h3><ul><li> Old reward: Pump-action shotgun and 12 red bullets</li><li> New reward: Pump-action shotgun, 12 red bullets, and 100 scrap</li></ul><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250922_230803_1Kl7Y5iB_mceu_58610426811758571682298.jpg\"></p><p> Missions are now not only more rewarding but also more varied. Players are given an additional incentive to complete tasks early in the wipe, as the rewards help them progress faster and gather resources. The addition of scrap is especially welcome—it\'s always in demand.</p><p> The new reward system clearly encourages active participation in missions. This may change the usual balance at the start of the wipe, as many will try to complete quests faster for the bonuses.</p><h2 id=\"rtupdate\"> Rust: RT Update – Sphere Recycler and New Puzzles</h2><h3> Recycler on the sphere</h3><p> The long-awaited Recycler has finally been added to <strong>the sphere</strong> . To reach it, you\'ll need to complete <strong>a puzzle with a green map</strong> . Inside, you\'ll find:</p><ul><li> processor,</li><li> two boxes with loot,</li><li> blue access card,</li><li> A fragment of a common blueprint for crafting <strong>the 2nd workbench</strong> . </li></ul><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250922_230921_P_OX83jy_mceu_96914806651758571760593.jpg\" alt=\"rust sphere\" width=\"496\" height=\"279\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250922_230935_WAS6ICAY_photo_2025-09-21_18-27-30.jpg\" alt=\"processor in the sphere\" width=\"539\" height=\"279\"></p><h3> Changes at the ferry terminal</h3><p> <strong>The ferry terminal</strong> has also been updated. <strong>A green map puzzle</strong> has now appeared there, and the reward for completing it includes:</p><ul><li> two boxes with valuable loot,</li><li> blue access card,</li><li> A fragment of a common blueprint for crafting a second workbench.</li></ul><p> The addition of a Recycler to the Sphere and new puzzles add more variety to the game. The Sphere now becomes an even more sought-after location, and the Ferry Terminal gains additional value. This also increases competition for control of key PTs, as the rewards significantly aid development in the early stages of a wipe. </p><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250922_231015_p7oTKuQB_mceu_69365112861758571814744.jpg\" width=\"732\" height=\"412\"></p><h2 id=\"performance\"> Performance and future plans</h2><p> After the latest patch, players noticed a drop in FPS. The developers confirmed the issues and promise optimizations this month. Furthermore, insiders reported that the naval update will be released in November. To improve performance, you can use our <a href=\"/posts/rust-news/rust-guides-tutorials-secrets-and-tactics/post-memory-and-fps-optimization-in-rust-a-complete-guide-to-setting-up-your-pc-graphics-and-teams\">game optimization guide</a> .</p><h2 id=\"summary\"> Results</h2><p> Rust is undergoing one of its most extensive changes in recent memory. The return of the blueprint system, drones with combat potential, new monuments, and item balancing could completely change the game\'s meta. Players can only wait for the updates to hit the main client.</p><p> Try out the new mechanics on our servers starting October 2: <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/servers\">https://prostoj.store/servers</a> .</p>'),
(18532, 'en-US', 'General ban list for {projectName} servers. Check the ban reason, server, and expiration date. The list is updated automatically.'),
(18533, 'en-US', 'Prohibit display in someone else\'s closet area'),
(18534, 'en-US', 'Guide | Underwater Labs | Rust, Labs, Loot'),
(18535, 'en-US', 'How to loot underwater labs in Rust.'),
(18536, 'en-US', '<h1>Underwater Labs in Rust <br><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250924_222554_-caliBtO_mceclip0.png\" width=\"801\" height=\"397\"></h1><h2> Types of complexes</h2><p> There are no specific types of underwater laboratories. Each facility is <strong>randomly</strong> generated, and the layout of the rooms doesn\'t follow any pattern. Essentially, they are a collection of random modules connected by passages and tunnels.<br><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250924_222631_DzuGac0c_mceclip2.png\" width=\"801\" height=\"406\"></p><h2>Methods of penetration</h2><p> There are two ways to get to the underwater station:</p><ol><li> <strong>On a submarine</strong> —a team-based game. You need to find a suitable entrance through which the vehicle can pass.</li><li> <strong>Using a motorboat with scuba gear</strong> is a more dangerous method, but it doesn\'t require purchasing a submarine. A boat will quickly get you to the site, and scuba gear will allow you to dive and enter without the risk of suffocation.</li></ol><h2> Containers and their location</h2><p> Finding loot here isn\'t the easiest. Be sure to bring <em>a flashlight or other light source</em> , as the lighting is dim and some containers are hidden.</p><p> The lab contains both standard crates (military, elite, component, and fuel barrels) and unique <strong>yellow</strong> and <strong>blue</strong> containers. You can also find crates containing ammunition, food, and medical supplies.</p><p> Some containers are located in places where they can be easily missed, such as on overhead bins in cabins.</p><h3> Main loot zones</h3><ul><li> <strong>The main entrance block</strong> contains barrels and canisters with fuel.</li><li> <strong>Additional block</strong> - blue and yellow boxes.</li><li> <strong>Medical compartment</strong> - containers with medicines and food.</li><li> <strong>Cabins, captain\'s quarters, command center, engine room</strong> - almost all types of boxes, except for military and elite.</li></ul><p> <strong>A green access card</strong> can be found in the engine room and security unit. In the former, it\'s on a workbench on level 3; in the latter, it\'s on the floor next to a locker.</p><p> Some valuable containers are hidden behind closed doors that open after solving small puzzles. These are significantly less challenging than those at the cosmodrome. <br><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250924_222724_x0seI_Hw_mceclip3.png\" width=\"645\" height=\"311\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250924_222756_nufC_Ouf_mceclip4.png\" width=\"604\" height=\"311\"></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250924_222911_sHMdCAbX_mceclip5.png\" width=\"646\" height=\"324\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250924_222926_R2soG0Iy_mceclip6.png\" width=\"629\" height=\"324\"></p><h2> Opponents</h2><p> <strong>Underwater scientists</strong> patrol the laboratory grounds, armed with an M92 Beretta pistol and an MP5A4 submachine gun. It\'s recommended to ensure you have high-quality equipment before heading out. </p><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250924_223010_qSOsiSwQ_mceclip7.png\" width=\"649\" height=\"333\"></p><h2> Access cards<br><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250924_223433_vsF-D1E4_mceclip9.png\" width=\"328\" height=\"328\"></h2><p>For a complete exploration of the complex, take:</p><ul><li> several fuses,</li><li> two green cards,</li><li> one blue card,</li><li> red card.</li></ul><p> This set is enough to open all doors.</p><h2> Map of the area</h2><p> The global map only shows the approximate locations of entry points. The internal structure of the location cannot be determined from the map—it\'s too small.</p><h2> Security camera codes<br><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20250924_223104_GfDdLOx7_mceclip8.png\" width=\"518\" height=\"273\"></h2><p>Most compartments are equipped with cameras with <strong>random names</strong> (room name + 4 digits). The security room has a computer station where all active cameras are already entered. By rewriting their codes, you can gain remote access from your database.</p><p> Code examples:</p><ul><li> AUXPOWER1224</li><li> LOCKERROOM1194</li><li> HALLWAY1230</li><li> LOCKERROOM1189</li><li> OPERATIONS1206</li><li> LOCKERROOM1188</li><li> LAB1169</li><li> INFIRMARY1182</li><li> LOCKERROOM1193</li></ul>'),
(18537, 'en-US', 'Global Wipe | RUST Update | The Hunger Games Event'),
(18538, 'en-US', 'A wipe on all servers, a game update, and a grand tournament!'),
