(18542, 'en-US', 'Rust\'s New Blueprint Fragment System and Workbenches: My Thoughts After the October Update'),
(18543, 'en-US', 'A detailed breakdown of the October 2025 Rust update: the new blueprint fragment system, revised requirements for T2 and T3 workbenches, reworked loot, and my personal impressions of the update.'),
(18544, 'en-US', '<p>In October 2025, Rust received one of the most extensive updates in recent years. We\'ve already covered all the changes in detail—from <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/posts/rust-news/update/post-rust-october-2025-update-blueprints-c4-drones-volcano-and-new-mechanics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">new blueprints to the volcano and C4 drones</a> . Here, I\'ll share my impressions and emotions regarding <strong>the new blueprint fragment system</strong> and the new workbench crafting system.</p><hr><h2> ? Navigation</h2><ul><li> <a href=\"#about\">What are drawing fragments?</a></li><li> <a href=\"#types\">Types of fragments and where to find them</a></li><li> <a href=\"#workbenches\">New requirements for workbenches</a></li><li> <a href=\"#monuments\">Changes to monuments</a></li><li> <a href=\"#proscons\">Pros and cons</a></li><li> <a href=\"#conclusion\">Conclusion and my feelings</a></li></ul><hr><h2 id=\"about\"> ? What are drawing fragments?</h2><p> After the update, Scrap is no longer the only way to advance in crafting. <strong>Blueprint Fragments</strong> are now available—special items that must be found in the world. Without them, you won\'t be able to assemble a T2 or T3 Workbench, even if you have a mountain of scrap metal. They can\'t be crafted or sold, and each find feels like real progress.</p><p> If you want to see how this all fits into the overall context of the patch, here\'s <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/posts/rust-news/update/post-rust-october-2025-update-blueprints-c4-drones-volcano-and-new-mechanics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">our detailed overview of the full Rust October 2025 update</a> .</p><hr><h2 id=\"types\"> ? Types of fragments and where to find them</h2><table><thead><tr><th> Fragment type</th><th> Where to find</th><th> What is it for?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> <strong>Basic Blueprint Fragment</strong></td><td> On the table with the red card in the blue room (puzzle room). Also found in green and red zones.</td><td> You need 5 pieces to create Workbench T2.</td></tr><tr><td> <strong>Advanced Blueprint Fragment</strong></td><td> Drops from elite crates and hackable containers. Look for them in the Launch Site, Military Tunnels, and Missile Silo.</td><td> You need 5 pieces to create Workbench T3.</td></tr></tbody></table><p> <em>There are rumors that in the future it will be possible to combine basic fragments into advanced ones, but this has not yet been implemented.</em></p><hr><h2 id=\"workbenches\"> ⚙️ New requirements for workbenches</h2><p> Scrap is now just part of the recipe. Fragments have become a mandatory element of crafting:</p><table><thead><tr><th> Workbench</th><th> New requirements</th><th> Previously it was required</th><th> Comment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Workbench T2</td><td> 5 Basic Blueprint Fragments + 250 Scrap</td><td> ~500 Scrap (without fragments)</td><td> Fragments are a required component, Scrap has been reduced.</td></tr><tr><td> Workbench T3</td><td> 5 Advanced Blueprint Fragments + 500 Scrap</td><td> ~1250 Scrap</td><td> Fragments are only needed for creation, not for repair.</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><h2 id=\"monuments\"> ?️ Changes to monuments</h2><p> With the introduction of fragments, the developers reworked the loot in monuments—now you can\'t get very far without raids.</p><ul><li> Fragments are guaranteed to appear on tables with cards (especially in the blue room).</li><li> Elite and hackable containers give an increased chance of receiving Advanced Fragments.</li><li> Loot distribution has become less predictable—routes need to be reconsidered.</li><li> Some puzzles have become more difficult (especially in Missile Silo).</li></ul><hr><h2 id=\"proscons\"> ? Pros and cons</h2><h3> Pros:</h3><ul><li> Rust once again encourages exploration and risk.</li><li> Every discovery of a fragment feels like an achievement.</li><li> Monuments have become really important - PvP is in full swing there.</li><li> Progress has become deeper and more interesting.</li></ul><h3> Cons:</h3><ul><li> It\'s more difficult for beginners now - initial progress is slow.</li><li> The rarity of fragments depends on the map - it is not always balanced.</li><li> The RNG and competition for loot can be annoying at first.</li></ul><hr><h2 id=\"conclusion\"> ? Conclusion and personal impressions</h2><p> When I first built Workbench T2 after the update, I honestly felt a sense of victory. Rust forces you <strong>to take action</strong> again, not just farm Scrap alone. It\'s a step toward dynamism, risk, and true survival.</p><p> If you want to know what else is in the October update, read the full review on Prostoj.Store: <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/posts/rust-news/update/post-rust-october-2025-update-blueprints-c4-drones-volcano-and-new-mechanics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rust 2025 October Update: Blueprints, C4 Drones, Volcano, and New Mechanics</a> .</p><p> See you in the world of Rust – and may luck be on your side, survivor!</p>'),
(18545, 'en-US', '<p>In October 2025, Rust received one of the most extensive updates in recent years. We\'ve already covered all the changes in detail—from <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/posts/rust-news/update/post-rust-october-2025-update-blueprints-c4-drones-volcano-and-new-mechanics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">new blueprints to the volcano and C4 drones</a> . Here, I\'ll share my impressions and emotions regarding <strong>the new blueprint fragment system</strong> and the new workbench crafting system.</p><hr><h2> ? Navigation</h2><ul><li> <a href=\"#about\">What are drawing fragments?</a></li><li> <a href=\"#types\">Types of fragments and where to find them</a></li><li> <a href=\"#workbenches\">New requirements for workbenches</a></li><li> <a href=\"#monuments\">Changes to monuments</a></li><li> <a href=\"#proscons\">Pros and cons</a></li><li> <a href=\"#conclusion\">Conclusion and my feelings</a></li></ul><hr><h2 id=\"about\"> ? What are drawing fragments?</h2><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20251008_035936_J7uKES5m_mceu_1455974611759885174499.jpg\"></p><p> After the update, Scrap is no longer the only way to advance in crafting. <strong>Blueprint Fragments</strong> are now available—special items that must be found in the world. Without them, you won\'t be able to assemble a T2 or T3 Workbench, even if you have a mountain of scrap metal. They can\'t be crafted or sold, and each find feels like real progress.</p><p> If you want to see how this all fits into the overall context of the patch, here\'s <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/posts/rust-news/update/post-rust-october-2025-update-blueprints-c4-drones-volcano-and-new-mechanics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">our detailed overview of the full Rust October 2025 update</a> .</p><hr><h2 id=\"types\"> ? Types of fragments and where to find them</h2><table><thead><tr><th> Fragment type</th><th> Where to find</th><th> What is it for?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> <strong>Basic Blueprint Fragment</strong></td><td> On the table with the red card in the blue room (puzzle room). Also found in green and red zones.</td><td> You need 5 pieces to create Workbench T2.</td></tr><tr><td> <strong>Advanced Blueprint Fragment</strong></td><td> Drops from elite crates and hackable containers. Look for them in the Launch Site, Military Tunnels, and Missile Silo.</td><td> You need 5 pieces to create Workbench T3.</td></tr></tbody></table><p> <em>There are rumors that in the future it will be possible to combine basic fragments into advanced ones, but this has not yet been implemented.</em></p><hr><h2 id=\"workbenches\"> ⚙️ New requirements for workbenches </h2><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20251008_035916_Tg3XB7M1_1-2_0.jpg\" alt=\"Rust Vertsaki\" width=\"903\" height=\"508\"><br> Scrap is now just part of the recipe. Fragments have become a mandatory element of crafting:</p><table><thead><tr><th> Workbench</th><th> New requirements</th><th> Previously it was required</th><th> Comment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Workbench T2</td><td> 5 Basic Blueprint Fragments + 250 Scrap</td><td> ~500 Scrap (without fragments)</td><td> Fragments are a required component, Scrap has been reduced.</td></tr><tr><td> Workbench T3</td><td> 5 Advanced Blueprint Fragments + 500 Scrap</td><td> ~1250 Scrap</td><td> Fragments are only needed for creation, not for repair.</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><h2 id=\"monuments\"> ?️ Changes to monuments</h2><p> With the introduction of fragments, the developers reworked the loot in monuments—now you can\'t get very far without raids.</p><ul><li> Fragments are guaranteed to appear on tables with cards (especially in the blue room).</li><li> Elite and hackable containers give an increased chance of receiving Advanced Fragments.</li><li> Loot distribution has become less predictable—routes need to be reconsidered.</li><li> Some puzzles have become more difficult (especially in Missile Silo).</li></ul><hr><h2 id=\"proscons\"> ? Pros and cons</h2><h3> Pros:</h3><ul><li> Rust once again encourages exploration and risk.</li><li> Every discovery of a fragment feels like an achievement.</li><li> Monuments have become really important - PvP is in full swing there.</li><li> Progress has become deeper and more interesting.</li></ul><h3> Cons:</h3><ul><li> It\'s more difficult for beginners now - initial progress is slow.</li><li> The rarity of fragments depends on the map - it is not always balanced.</li><li> The RNG and competition for loot can be annoying at first.</li></ul><hr><h2 id=\"conclusion\"> ? Conclusion and personal impressions</h2><p> When I first built Workbench T2 after the update, I honestly felt a sense of victory. Rust forces you <strong>to take action</strong> again, not just farm Scrap alone. It\'s a step toward dynamism, risk, and true survival.</p><p> If you want to know what else is in the October update, read the full review on Prostoj.Store: <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/posts/rust-news/update/post-rust-october-2025-update-blueprints-c4-drones-volcano-and-new-mechanics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rust 2025 October Update: Blueprints, C4 Drones, Volcano, and New Mechanics</a> .</p><p> See you in the world of Rust – and may luck be on your side, survivor!</p>'),
(18546, 'en-US', 'Global Wipe | RUST Update | The Hunger Games Event'),
(18547, 'en-US', 'Rust x Warhammer 40,000: Death Korps of Krieg – What\'s in the New DLC?'),
(18548, 'en-US', 'The new Rust × Warhammer 40,000: Death Korps of Krieg DLC releases on October 23. The pack includes a hazmat suit, chainsword, shotgun, backpack, and Krieg-themed barrels. Learn more about the contents and where to buy.'),
(18549, 'en-US', '<p>The <strong>Rust — Warhammer Pack,</strong> featuring <em>the Death Korps of Krieg</em> aesthetic, is now available on Steam. Expected release date: <strong>October 23rd</strong> .</p><h2> Contents of the set</h2><ul><li> Death Korps of Krieg hazmat suit</li><li> The Death Korps of Krieg chainsword <span title=\"essentially a themed skin\">is likely a reskin of the chainsaw.</span></li><li> Death Korps of Krieg shotgun</li><li> Death Korps of Krieg-themed barrels/storage containers</li><li> Death Korps of Krieg Backpack</li></ul><p> This set focuses on visual customization and the atmosphere of the Warhammer 40,000 universe. It\'s a great option if you want to design your character and base in the rugged style of Krieg.</p><h2> Where to buy</h2><p> Official Steam DLC page: <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/3891560/Rust_Warhammer_Pack/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Rust — Warhammer Pack (Steam)</a></p><h2> Where to watch for the exit</h2><p> Keep an eye on the DLC page and the Rust community for updates—content and details may be updated before the release date.</p><hr><p> For more information on Rust DLC and current packs, see <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/posts/rust-news/rust-guides-tutorials-secrets-and-tactics/post-rust-dlc--full-guide-what-they-are-what-they-give-where-to-buy-and-how-to-save\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the full Rust DLC guide on Prostoj.Store</a> .</p>'),
(18550, 'en-US', '<p>The <strong>Rust — Warhammer Pack,</strong> featuring <em>the Death Korps of Krieg</em> aesthetic, is now available on Steam. Expected release date: <strong>October 23rd</strong> . <br><br><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20251010_100143_60hylA6y_ss_9db7a52494dca89d0df88474971e6351dd8051e3.1920x1080.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"960\" height=\"540\"></p><h2> Contents of the set</h2><ul><li> Death Korps of Krieg hazmat suit</li><li> The Death Korps of Krieg chainsword <span title=\"essentially a themed skin\">is likely a reskin of the chainsaw.</span></li><li> Death Korps of Krieg shotgun</li><li> Death Korps of Krieg-themed barrels/storage containers</li><li> Death Korps of Krieg Backpack</li></ul><p> This set focuses on visual customization and the atmosphere of the Warhammer 40,000 universe. It\'s a great option if you want to design your character and base in the rugged style of Krieg. <br><br></p><p><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20251010_100204_qu58RRUG_mceu_91191657311760079719306.jpg\" width=\"505\" height=\"284\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20251010_100219_V_Akdbb6_ss_052ef01bf19c0e88aa56d7e08bd9df315e6a3292.1920x1080.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"503\" height=\"283\"><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20251010_100239_Wn1Jaqap_ss_a6cca20c8238e76423c4dc81c1f8fbd468fa5393.1920x1080.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"508\" height=\"286\"></p><h2> Where to buy</h2><p> Official Steam DLC page: <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/3891560/Rust_Warhammer_Pack/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">Rust — Warhammer Pack (Steam)</a></p><h2> Where to watch for the exit</h2><p> Keep an eye on the DLC page and the Rust community for updates—content and details may be updated before the release date.</p><hr><p> For more information on Rust DLC and current packs, see <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/posts/rust-news/rust-guides-tutorials-secrets-and-tactics/post-rust-dlc--full-guide-what-they-are-what-they-give-where-to-buy-and-how-to-save\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the full Rust DLC guide on Prostoj.Store</a> .</p>'),
(18551, 'en-US', '<p>DLC (Downloadable Content) are extensions to Rust that add unique items, styles, musical instruments, voice abilities, and even visual enhancements to buildings. Below, we\'ve compiled a complete list of all available DLC as of 2025.</p><h2> ? Quick links</h2><ul><li> <a href=\"#jungle\">Jungle Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#frontier\">Frontier Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#sunburn\">Sunburn Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#arctic\">Arctic Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#instrument\">Instrument Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#voice\">Voice Props</a></li><li> <a href=\"#ancient\">Ancient Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#abyss\">Abyss Pack</a></li><li> <a href=\"#pilot\">Pilot Pack DLC (Pilot Hazmat)</a></li><li> <a href=\"#warhammer\">Warhammer Pack</a></li></ul><hr><!-- Warhammer DLC --><h2 id=\"warhammer\"> ⚔️ Rust × Warhammer 40,000: Death Korps of Krieg </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"/uploads/blog/20251010_100447_Dz4I73oq_ss_9db7a52494dca89d0df88474971e6351dd8051e3.1920x1080.jpg\" alt=\"Rust Warhammer Pack DLC\"></p><p> <strong>Release date:</strong> October 23, 2025</p><p> The Rust × Warhammer 40,000 co-op DLC brings the grim atmosphere <em>of the Death Korps of Krieg</em> to the harsh world of Rust. The pack includes:</p><ul><li> Death Korps of Krieg hazmat suit</li><li> Chainsword - likely a reskin of the chainsaw</li><li> Death Korps of Krieg shotgun</li><li> Barrels/storage containers</li><li> Death Korps of Krieg Backpack</li></ul><p> This set is designed purely for customization and does not provide any combat advantages, but is ideal for Warhammer fans and collectors of rare skins.</p><p> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/3891560/Rust_Warhammer_Pack/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">? Buy Rust — Warhammer Pack on Steam</a></p><hr><h2 id=\"jungle\"> ? Jungle Pack DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/jungle-pack-og.jpg\" alt=\"Jungle Pack DLC\"></p><p> Decorate your base in tropical style. Jungle-inspired furniture, decor, and textures.</p><ul><li> Palm bed</li><li> Bamboo chairs and tables</li><li> Reptile Wall Mask</li><li> Wooden totem torches</li></ul><h2 id=\"frontier\"> ? Frontier Pack DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/rust_frontiersman_hero_02.jpg\" alt=\"Frontier Pack DLC\"></p><p> The barrel DLC is one of the most useful sets for PvE and RP bases. It\'s themed after the Wild West.</p><ul><li> <strong>Barrel Storage</strong> - a spacious storage unit (like a large box)</li><li> Saloon Door - double-leaf cowboy door</li><li> Chandelier, wooden furniture, gun rack</li></ul><h2 id=\"sunburn\"> ? Sunburn Pack DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/sunburn-header.jpg\" alt=\"Sunburn Pack DLC\"></p><p> Summer aesthetic: a beach vacation at your own base. Pairs perfectly with RP.</p><ul><li> Inflatable pool</li><li> Sun loungers, umbrellas</li><li> Towel (spawnpoint)</li><li> Clothing - glasses, t-shirts, swimsuits</li></ul><h2 id=\"arctic\"> ❄ Arctic Pack DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/iceassaultrifle.jpg\" alt=\"Arctic Pack DLC\"></p><p> DLC for snow biomes. Items look like expedition gear.</p><ul><li> Arctic Hazmat Suit</li><li> Fur hoods, windings</li><li> Snow camouflage</li></ul><h2 id=\"instrument\"> ? Instrument Pack DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/ss_383b5d3c204dd6fd7dc6eac1643f14de35293363.1920x1080.jpg\" alt=\"Instrument Pack DLC\"></p><p> The first music DLC in Rust. Allows you to play instruments manually or with a MIDI keyboard.</p><ul><li> Guitar, bass guitar</li><li> Xylophone, keys, drums</li><li> Trumpet, saxophone</li><li> Bongo, pots</li></ul><h2 id=\"voice\"> ? Voice Props DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/Rust-Voice-Props-DLC-803x452.jpg\" alt=\"Voice Props DLC\"></p><p> An audio supplement for lovers of creativity and atmosphere.</p><ul><li> Speakers (sound reproduction)</li><li> Cassette recorder and cassettes</li><li> Radio and voice amplifiers</li><li> Microphones, disco lights</li></ul><h2 id=\"ancient\"> ? Ancient Pack DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/cDjTrmjWNic3QEmhkeWuLQ.jpg\" alt=\"Ancient Pack DLC\"></p><p> Stylization of ancient civilizations: columns, stone patterns, tarnished metal.</p><ul><li> Stone walls with symbols</li><li> Clay and bronze elements</li><li> Torches and columns</li></ul><h2 id=\"abyss\"> ? Abyss Pack DLC </h2><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/F0X0GjYaQAAl9MG.jpg\" alt=\"Abyss Pack DLC\"></p><p> Underwater theme. Perfect for ocean bases and deep caves.</p><ul><li> Helmet with backlight</li><li> Dark suits with steel accents</li><li> Decorations for underwater buildings</li></ul><h2 id=\"pilot\"> ✈️ Pilot Pack DLC (Pilot Hazmat)</h2><p> The latest <strong>Pilot DLC</strong> adds aviation-themed elements to Rust. This pack combines <em>a mystical atmosphere</em> with military aesthetics. Visual effects and new sounds make it one of the most atmospheric and unique packs of 2025.</p><p> The update will be available from August 7, 2025. </p><p><img style=\"max-width: 100%; width: 600px;\" src=\"https://storage.prostoj.store/blog/dlc/photo_2025-07-23_10-18-22.jpg\" alt=\"Rust DLC Pilot Hazmat – weapons, seat, and aviation-themed skins\"></p><p> <strong>What\'s included in the DLC:</strong></p><ul><li> <strong>M15 (Pawn Reskin)</strong> - A unique weapon skin with <em>glow-in-the-dark effects</em> and reworked firing sounds.</li><li> <strong>Pilot Hazmat</strong> is a suit skin with flight gear, helmet, and breathing mask.</li><li> <strong>This combination lock skin</strong> is styled like an aircraft panel and looks both technologically advanced and unique.</li><li> <strong>The skin for the small crate</strong> is a discreet dark design with details of an air container.</li><li> <strong>The pilot\'s chair</strong> is a massive one with metal accents and blue glow, reminiscent of an ice throne. It fits perfectly into command bases.</li></ul><p> <strong>For whom:</strong> For collectors, headquarters builders, and players who value unique appearance and sound effects.</p><hr><h2> ? Where can I buy the Rust DLC?</h2><ul><li> <strong>Steam</strong> - all official DLC is sold on the game page.</li><li> <strong>Rust DLC Bundle</strong> - sometimes available during sales.</li><li> <strong>FunPay</strong> - accounts with already activated DLC (unofficial).</li></ul><h2> ? Buying tips</h2><ol><li> Expect seasonal discounts (summer, fall, winter, spring).</li><li> Buy DLC as a set.</li><li> Do not use DLC Unlocker - it violates Steam\'s terms of service and may result in a ban.</li></ol><h2> ✅ Conclusion</h2><p> The most useful DLCs are <strong>Frontier (barrels)</strong> , <strong>Arctic (cold protection)</strong> , <strong>Instrument</strong> , and <strong>Voice Props</strong> for creativity. The rest are for atmosphere and base customization. Choose based on your playstyle!</p>'),
(18552, 'en-US', 'Stickers'),
(18553, 'en-US', 'Rust — November 2025 Update (Naval) + Warhammer 40,000 DLC: What\'s New and Where to Play'),
(18554, 'en-US', 'A full breakdown of the November Rust 2025 update: the Naval update, what\'s already on the stage branch, vehicle balance, and a review of the Warhammer 40,000 DLC. Connect to our servers and test it out.');
INSERT INTO `language_translate` (`id`, `language`, `translation`) VALUES
(18555, 'en-US', '<p class=\"muted\">Updated: October 2025. We expect the main patch to be released in November 2025; the test is already available on the stage branch. </p><figure><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20251015_150102_u5B5Jud1_G26B__BWkAA6yuz.jpeg\" alt=\"Rust\'s Naval Update: Deep Sea, Modular Boats, and Floating Cities\" width=\"576\" height=\"323\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> Naval: deep sea, modular boats, new zones and water activities.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"toc\"> <strong>Content</strong><ol><li> <a href=\"#summary\">Briefly about the main thing</a></li><li> <a href=\"#naval\">Naval Update</a></li><li> <a href=\"#air\">Air transport balance</a></li><li> <a href=\"#warhammer\">Warhammer 40,000 DLC: What\'s Included</a></li><li> <a href=\"#how-to-test\">How to test on stage</a></li><li> <a href=\"#servers\">Where to play: our servers</a></li><li> <a href=\"#faq\">FAQ</a></li></ol></div><h2 id=\"summary\"> Briefly about the main thing</h2><ul><li> Key elements <strong>of Naval</strong> are already available on the stage branch: modular boats, deep sea, floating cities, ghost ships, and scientist patrol boats.</li><li> Changes are being made to <strong>air transport</strong> and interaction with flares.</li><li> <strong>The Warhammer 40,000 DLC</strong> is getting ready for release, bringing new cosmetics and items. For more details and an analysis, check out our article: <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/posts/rust-news/update/post-rust-x-warhammer-40000-death-korps-of-krieg--what39s-in-the-new-dlc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rust × Warhammer 40,000 – What\'s in the New DLC</a> .</li></ul><h2 id=\"naval\"> Naval Update: What\'s Already Been Seen in Test </h2><figure><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20251015_150121_CGmLw45U_G26BNXRWYAA5Kr5.jpeg\" alt=\"Modular boats in Rust: hull assembly, power module, deck elements\" width=\"746\" height=\"417\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> Modular boats: we assemble a configuration for farming, raiding, or deep-sea expeditions.</figcaption></figure><h3> Main features</h3><ul><li> <strong>Modular boats</strong> : hull + power module + deck elements, combat configuration is possible.</li><li> <strong>Deep Sea</strong> : A new zone beyond the familiar map with increased risks and rewards.</li><li> <strong>Floating Cities</strong> : Compact clusters of interest on the water, vendors/content depend on the build.</li><li> <strong>Ghost ships</strong> : events and rare loot, threat variability.</li><li> <strong>Scientists\' Patrol Boats</strong> : Active AI patrols, dynamic combat on the water.</li></ul><table><thead><tr><th> Component</th><th> What is this</th><th> Practical benefits</th><th> Status on stage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Modular boats</td><td> Water transport constructor from sections</td><td> Adaptation for farming, PVP, and long-range raids</td><td> <span class=\"badge\">Available</span></td></tr><tr><td> Deep Sea</td><td> Zone beyond the edge of the map, increased risks</td><td> Rare events, unique loot</td><td> <span class=\"badge\">Available</span></td></tr><tr><td> Floating cities</td><td> Clusters of POIs on water</td><td> Loot routes, encounters, risk/reward</td><td> <span class=\"badge\">Partially</span></td></tr><tr><td> Ghost ships</td><td> Events at sea</td><td> Rare loot, PVE/PVP scenes</td><td> <span class=\"badge\">Test</span></td></tr><tr><td> Scientists\' patrol boats</td><td> AI activity on water</td><td> Living Sea, challenges for farm routes</td><td> <span class=\"badge\">Available</span></td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"note\"> Note: The feature set on the stage branch is subject to change. In individual builds, some content may be disabled or replaced with placeholders.</div><h2 id=\"air\"> Air transport balance and flares </h2><figure><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20251015_151047_OzNmNkR1_Screenshot_85-1024x567.png\" alt=\"Aircraft Balance: Minicopter, Clan Helicopter, Attack Helicopter\" width=\"748\" height=\"414\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> Adjustments to flair and crew capabilities impact the aerial combat meta.</figcaption></figure><p> The testing phase includes adjustments to the interaction between aircraft, flares, and MANPADS. Below is a summary of what is already being discussed and finalized at the stage.</p><table><thead><tr><th> Technique</th><th> Change</th><th> What does it affect?</th><th> Comment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Minicopter</td><td> Slot/mechanics for flairs</td><td> Countermeasure against homing missiles</td><td> Open Skies Survival Balance</td></tr><tr><td> Clan helicopter</td><td> Flare support</td><td> Protection on routes to raids</td><td> Fewer one-shot situations</td></tr><tr><td> Attack helicopter</td><td> Restrictions on passenger manual throwing of flairs</td><td> Reducing abuse by the crew</td><td> Pilot/Defense Systems Role Rebalance</td></tr><tr><td> Balloon</td><td> Engine shutdown to reset the grip</td><td> Tactical countermeasure against missiles</td><td> Delay in activation after stopping</td></tr></tbody></table><p> The bottom line for the meta: Flares remain an important countermeasure, but their use is becoming more meaningful and less prone to abuse. Piloting and timing are becoming increasingly important.</p><h2 id=\"warhammer\"> Warhammer 40,000: Death Korps of Krieg DLC – What\'s Included </h2><figure><img src=\"/uploads/blog/20251015_150913_aeDToUpU_ss_2b30d1b697cb2273a8590ac44f6bf420m_7550d31d.1920x1080.jpg\" alt=\"Rust x Warhammer 40,000: Death Korps of Krieg Skins and Items\" width=\"782\" height=\"440\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> Warhammer 40,000 DLC: stylized equipment and storage for the Death Korps of Krieg.</figcaption></figure><p> A cosmetic pack based on the Warhammer 40,000 universe is expected to arrive separately from the game patch. We\'ve covered its contents and features in detail here: <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/posts/rust-news/update/post-rust-x-warhammer-40000-death-korps-of-krieg--what39s-in-the-new-dlc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rust × Warhammer 40,000 – What\'s in the New DLC</a> .</p><table><thead><tr><th> Element</th><th> Description</th><th> Type</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td> Krieg protective suit</td><td> The appearance of a typical hazmat with a gas mask and overcoat</td><td> Skin</td></tr><tr><td> Krieg\'s Backpack</td><td> Death Korps-themed field backpack</td><td> Skin/Item</td></tr><tr><td> Krieg\'s Chainsword</td><td> A chainsaw skin with brutal visuals</td><td> Tool skin</td></tr><tr><td> Krieg\'s Shotgun</td><td> Warhammer 40,000-themed firearm skin</td><td> Weapon skin</td></tr><tr><td> Krieg storage containers</td><td> Two Krieg style storage barrels</td><td> Skin for storage</td></tr></tbody></table><p> This set is designed for fans of the universe and those who want to stand out online with a recognizable visual style. It pairs well with dark bases, industrial, and militaristic builds.</p><h2 id=\"how-to-test\"> How to test Naval on stage</h2><ol><li> Switch to the <strong>Staging</strong> branch on Steam for Rust.</li><li> Log in to a test server or single session.</li><li> For deep sea, use server/developer utility commands if they are available in the build.</li></ol><p> Example of auxiliary commands for a local test or server with rights:</p><pre> <code>ent spawn assets/content/vehicles/boats/modular_boat.prefab ent spawn assets/content/vehicles/boats/rhib/rhib.prefab # Дополнительные команды зависят от билда и прав на сервере</code></pre><p> Some builds support entering the deep sea zone through special points. If your server has a command, check the server description for it.</p><h2 id=\"servers\"> Where to play: our servers</h2><p> We\'re preparing the infrastructure for Naval and actively monitoring the stage updates to ensure a smooth update. Join us for the next wipe:</p><p> <a class=\"cta\" href=\"https://prostoj.store/servers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Go to the website and select a server</a></p><h2 id=\"faq\"> FAQ</h2><details><summary> When will the main Naval patch be released?</summary><div> Expected for November 2025. Some functionality is already available on the stage branch to give the developers time to polish the build.</div></details><details><summary> Is it worth preparing separate bases for Naval?</summary><div> Yes. The new water meta will add farming routes, events, and risks. Plan ahead for water access points, a hangar/dock, fuel caches, and boat slots.</div></details><details><summary> Do I need to purchase the Warhammer DLC to access the Naval content?</summary><div> No. The DLC is a cosmetic addition. Naval is part of a free game update. <a href=\"https://prostoj.store/posts/rust-news/update/post-rust-x-warhammer-40000-death-korps-of-krieg--what39s-in-the-new-dlc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">A detailed review of the DLC is available here: prostoj.store</a> .</div></details><hr><p> If you\'re a server administrator testing a build, monitor log messages, plugin compatibility, and the load on coastal clusters. Players are advised to update clients, check their cache, and free up space for new assets.</p>');
